place in Boston. Can't make it.

4131
03:36:12,498 --> 03:36:14,665
What? No.

4132
03:36:15,207 --> 03:36:16,290
Okay.

4133
03:36:16,373 --> 03:36:19,207
No problem. No problem.
Dean, you can handle all his stuff, okay?

4134
03:36:19,290 --> 03:36:22,290
No, I would be all over that,
but I am road-tripping

4135
03:36:22,373 --> 03:36:24,873
- down to New York tomorrow with Bella.
- Oh, no, dude.

4136
03:36:24,957 --> 03:36:27,207
- No, no, no, no, no, no, no.
- Blackout Wednesday, dude.

4137
03:36:27,290 --> 03:36:30,832
Drinksgiving? Why would I be drunk here
when I could be drunk there?

4138
03:36:30,915 --> 03:36:33,082
Sorry, bro. See you next year.

4139
03:36:34,082 --> 03:36:36,665
So, the friends
are abandoning Friendsgiving.

4140
03:36:36,748 --> 03:36:37,915
Who needs them?

4141
03:36:37,998 --> 03:36:40,748
Jules and I are here, it's gonna be
the perfect fucking Thanksgiving.

4142
03:36:40,832 --> 03:36:41,832
What do you need?

4143
03:36:42,748 --> 03:36:44,373
I'll send you my to-do list.

4144
03:36:45,748 --> 03:36:46,915
[phone chimes]

4145
03:36:52,082 --> 03:36:53,790
- [Logan] Damn.
- [Tucker] I know.

4146
03:36:53,873 --> 03:36:54,998
It's glorious.

4147
03:37:00,707 --> 03:37:03,707
I'm so depressed you're not coming
to Brooklyn with me this year.

4148
03:37:03,790 --> 03:37:06,040
Me, too.
But I want to be there for Garrett.

4149
03:37:06,123 --> 03:37:08,415
As much as I love
watching Aunt Kathy get drunk

4150
03:37:08,498 --> 03:37:10,373
and busting out her old cheer routine.

4151
03:37:10,457 --> 03:37:12,998
- God, old gal's still got the splits.
- [laughs]

4152
03:37:13,082 --> 03:37:15,582
It's your first Thanksgiving without Sean.
How are you doing?

4153
03:37:15,665 --> 03:37:17,832
Honestly, I am loving my single life.

4154
03:37:17,915 --> 03:37:21,040
I'm Yasmina in season two
of <i>Al Nisa Alashba</i>.

4155
03:37:21,790 --> 03:37:24,873
Doesn't she fall into a coma
for most of that season?

4156
03:37:24,957 --> 03:37:27,790
Yes, but before that,
she is single and thriving.

4157
03:37:27,873 --> 03:37:28,832
As am I.

4158
03:37:28,915 --> 03:37:33,082
Just not getting tied down,
focusing on myself and my acting.

4159
03:37:33,165 --> 03:37:35,332
- That's it.
- Well, I am proud of you.

4160
03:37:35,415 --> 03:37:36,748
Well, you, too.

4161
03:37:36,832 --> 03:37:40,332
Meeting Garrett's dad,
being a good girlfriend and shit.

4162
03:37:40,415 --> 03:37:42,582
- [both laugh]
- You nervous?

4163
03:37:42,665 --> 03:37:43,707
Uh, no.

4164
03:37:45,123 --> 03:37:46,623
I mean, he's famous, right?

4165
03:37:47,165 --> 03:37:50,665
Yeah, yeah, okay, I'm a little nervous,
but not because he's famous.

4166
03:37:50,748 --> 03:37:52,540
Just... I don't know.

4167
03:37:52,623 --> 03:37:55,832
The way Garrett talks about him,
he seems like really intense.

4168
03:37:55,915 --> 03:37:58,540
Yeah, I've seen him at games.
Does the man ever smile?

4169
03:37:58,623 --> 03:38:00,123
I don't think so.

4170
03:38:00,207 --> 03:38:01,373
Well, don't stress.

4171
03:38:01,457 --> 03:38:03,123
It's not about him liking you.

4172
03:38:03,207 --> 03:38:04,665
It's about Garrett.

4173
03:38:04,748 --> 03:38:06,248
And he already likes you.

4174
03:38:07,123 --> 03:38:10,832
Yeah, I just think it's really important
to Garrett that this goes well.

4175
03:38:10,915 --> 03:38:13,248
That's what relationships are for,
honey bun.

4176
03:38:13,332 --> 03:38:14,498
Supporting each other.

4177
03:38:14,582 --> 03:38:16,582
Helping each other grow as people.

4178
03:38:17,665 --> 03:38:19,873
It can't all be about sex and fun.

4179
03:38:19,957 --> 03:38:21,415
[cell phone vibrates]

4180
03:38:21,498 --> 03:38:23,748
Oh, shit. The bus is almost here.
Gotta go.

4181
03:38:23,832 --> 03:38:25,998
Well, no, Garrett can just drive you.

4182
03:38:26,082 --> 03:38:27,290
No, it's fine. I love a bus.

4183
03:38:27,373 --> 03:38:28,707
You hate a bus.

4184
03:38:28,790 --> 03:38:29,707
It's fine.

4185
03:38:29,790 --> 03:38:31,790
I love you. Happy Thanksgiving.

4186
03:38:31,873 --> 03:38:34,998
Love you. [laughs]

4187
03:38:51,873 --> 03:38:54,332
- [Tucker] 425 for how long?
- [Gail on phone] <i>Thirty minutes.</i>

4188
03:38:54,415 --> 03:38:56,998
<i>Use that time to prep the turkey
before it has to go in.</i>

4189
03:38:57,082 --> 03:38:59,123
<i>- And don't forget to--</i>
- Pat-dry the bird.

4190
03:38:59,207 --> 03:39:01,582
I know. I know. Can't be wet.

4191
03:39:01,665 --> 03:39:04,790
<i>Unless you want a crispy turkey
and no eyebrows like Uncle Pete.</i>

4192
03:39:04,873 --> 03:39:08,623
<i>And don't skimp on the marshmallows
for the sweet potato casserole.</i>

4193
03:39:08,707 --> 03:39:10,415
Ooh, slivers, dude.

4194
03:39:10,498 --> 03:39:12,290
Dude, slivers.

4195
03:39:12,373 --> 03:39:13,248
Just... easy.

4196
03:39:13,332 --> 03:39:14,415
- Yes, chef.
- There you go.

4197
03:39:15,082 --> 03:39:18,332
<i>Just remember to drop the turkey in
exactly one hour</i>

4198
03:39:18,415 --> 03:39:19,623
<i>before your sides are ready.</i>

4199
03:39:19,707 --> 03:39:21,040
One hour. Got it.

4200
03:39:21,123 --> 03:39:23,290
<i>First Thanksgiving
you're cooking all on your own.</i>

4201
03:39:23,373 --> 03:39:24,915
It's weird doing all this without you.

4202
03:39:24,998 --> 03:39:26,082
<i>Miss you, too, JT.</i>

4203
03:39:26,165 --> 03:39:27,498
<i>But I'm right there with you.</i>

4204
03:39:27,582 --> 03:39:31,498
<i>I can practically smell
the sweat and testosterone.</i>

4205
03:39:31,582 --> 03:39:32,998
- [laughs]
- Fair.

4206
03:39:33,082 --> 03:39:35,082
Just don't want to screw anything up.

4207
03:39:35,165 --> 03:39:37,457
- It has to be perfect.
<i>- No such thing.</i>

4208
03:39:37,540 --> 03:39:38,623
<i>It's not the food.</i>

4209
03:39:38,707 --> 03:39:41,123
<i>It's the comfort and love
that make the food.</i>

4210
03:39:41,207 --> 03:39:42,832
Did you just quote the Barefoot Contessa?

4211
03:39:42,915 --> 03:39:45,748
<i>Or did she quote me?
No way of knowing, is there?</i>

4212
03:39:45,832 --> 03:39:46,915
[laughs]

4213
03:39:46,998 --> 03:39:48,207
Gravy, gotta go.

4214
03:39:48,290 --> 03:39:49,498
<i>Love you, baby.</i>

4215
03:39:53,123 --> 03:39:56,415
Perfect. Yes. Yes.

4216
03:39:58,998 --> 03:40:00,415
Where were the marshmallows?

4217
03:40:00,498 --> 03:40:04,207
I just saw them five seconds ago.
Where could they possibly go?

4218
03:40:04,290 --> 03:40:06,248
One, two, three.

4219
03:40:06,332 --> 03:40:08,582
They were just here.

4220
03:40:08,665 --> 03:40:09,832
What are you doing?

4221
03:40:09,915 --> 03:40:11,457
Keeping our family tradition alive.

4222
03:40:11,540 --> 03:40:14,373
I'm trying to have a normal
Thanksgiving right now, okay?

4223
03:40:14,457 --> 03:40:16,748
What's normal? Turkey, pumpkin pie?

4224
03:40:16,832 --> 03:40:17,998
Boo, boring.

4225
03:40:18,082 --> 03:40:20,290
Say what you will about Mom,
we always had fun.

4226
03:40:20,373 --> 03:40:23,248
Okay, you have a very interesting,
selective memory.

4227
03:40:23,332 --> 03:40:25,873
Can't we just enjoy this, please?

4228
03:40:25,957 --> 03:40:28,165
You are ruining Tuck's Thanksgiving.

4229
03:40:28,248 --> 03:40:30,957
[Tucker] They were just here.
The marshmallows were just here.

4230
03:40:31,040 --> 03:40:33,082
Party people!

4231
03:40:33,165 --> 03:40:34,832
- Happy Thanksgiving!
- Oh! Birdie!

4232
03:40:34,915 --> 03:40:36,332
Nats! Thank God!

4233
03:40:36,415 --> 03:40:39,665
- I thought we'd have too much food.
- Not a chance. We brought friends.

4234
03:40:39,748 --> 03:40:41,082
And we brought wine.

4235
03:40:41,165 --> 03:40:43,540
Oh, six. Six more people.
Hi, Kendall. Great.

4236
03:40:43,623 --> 03:40:45,998
That's perfect, I can do that. Yeah.
Hi, how you doing?

4237
03:40:46,082 --> 03:40:47,415
- Hi. Hi.
- Hi, Tucker. Thanks for having us.

4238
03:40:47,498 --> 03:40:51,165
- [indistinct chatter]
- Good to see you.

4239
03:40:51,248 --> 03:40:53,998
Is it possible to double a sweet potato
casserole in one dish?

4240
03:40:54,082 --> 03:40:55,623
You're asking me?

4241
03:40:56,123 --> 03:40:57,165
I got this.

4242
03:40:58,123 --> 03:40:59,540
This is a bad idea.

4243
03:40:59,623 --> 03:41:01,165
[Hannah] Yeah, you're right.

4244
03:41:01,248 --> 03:41:03,165
Who brings a key lime pie to Thanksgiving?

4245
03:41:03,248 --> 03:41:05,040
Why didn't you stop me? Pumpkin?

4246
03:41:05,123 --> 03:41:07,373
Pumpkin is the thing.

4247
03:41:07,457 --> 03:41:08,957
Or maybe I should have brought wine.

4248
03:41:09,040 --> 03:41:10,832
I meant my dad, Wellsy.

4249
03:41:11,498 --> 03:41:13,457
- Oh, right.
- [both laugh]

4250
03:41:14,373 --> 03:41:16,832
And we can go at any point.

4251
03:41:16,915 --> 03:41:18,873
Just give me the signal,
and we'll get the fuck out.

4252
03:41:18,957 --> 03:41:20,665
- The signal?
- Yeah.

4253
03:41:20,748 --> 03:41:23,207
Like, I don't know,
squeeze my hand or something.

4254
03:41:23,290 --> 03:41:24,623
Once means you're good.

4255
03:41:24,707 --> 03:41:26,582
Two squeezes, and we're gone.

4256
03:41:26,665 --> 03:41:28,123
[laughs]

4257
03:41:29,748 --> 03:41:30,915
[sighs]

4258
03:41:30,998 --> 03:41:32,707
Or we go?

4259
03:41:37,207 --> 03:41:40,248
Or... Or we stay?
You gotta give me something here.

4260
03:41:40,332 --> 03:41:41,373
[laughs]

4261
03:41:41,457 --> 03:41:43,498
All right, we stay.

4262
03:41:43,582 --> 03:41:44,540
Okay.

4263
03:41:46,582 --> 03:41:48,998
First step, getting out the car.

4264
03:41:49,082 --> 03:41:51,248
- [laughs]
- Yeah.

4265
03:41:51,332 --> 03:41:52,707
[doorbell rings]

4266
03:41:54,248 --> 03:41:56,040
Garrett, you made it.

4267
03:41:56,123 --> 03:41:57,123
Dad.

4268
03:41:57,207 --> 03:41:58,582
And you must be Hannah.

4269
03:41:58,665 --> 03:42:00,415
- Glad to finally meet you.
- Hi.

4270
03:42:00,498 --> 03:42:02,540
Sorry, I'd shake your hand, but--

4271
03:42:02,623 --> 03:42:03,748
Oh, I'll take that.

4272
03:42:03,832 --> 03:42:04,957
Pie!

4273
03:42:05,582 --> 03:42:08,373
Oh, it's key lime.
You love key lime.

4274
03:42:08,457 --> 03:42:11,123
- He loves key lime.
- I do, it's the superior pie, thank you.

4275
03:42:11,207 --> 03:42:13,457
Well, don't let the poor kids
freeze out there.

4276
03:42:13,540 --> 03:42:14,582
Come in.

4277
03:42:15,248 --> 03:42:17,332
I'm gonna put this in the fridge.

4278
03:42:17,415 --> 03:42:18,790
I'll take your coats.

4279
03:42:18,873 --> 03:42:20,082
Thank you.

4280
03:42:21,790 --> 03:42:23,165
Thanks.

4281
03:42:24,998 --> 03:42:26,332
[Hannah sighs]

4282
03:42:26,415 --> 03:42:28,332
It's a nice house.

4283
03:42:28,415 --> 03:42:30,040
- Yeah.
- [laughs]

4284
03:42:31,290 --> 03:42:33,915
Aw! Look at you.

4285
03:42:36,915 --> 03:42:37,873
Oh.

4286
03:42:42,998 --> 03:42:45,082
They look alike, don't they?

4287
03:42:45,165 --> 03:42:47,498
It's uncanny.

4288
03:42:47,582 --> 03:42:49,457
I'm so glad you're here, Garrett.

4289
03:42:49,540 --> 03:42:51,790
I can't wait to hear
all about how the season's going.

4290
03:42:51,873 --> 03:42:53,123
[laughs]

4291
03:42:53,207 --> 03:42:54,832
Come on, I'll put the game on.

4292
03:42:54,915 --> 03:42:56,123
It's you versus me, kid.

4293
03:42:56,207 --> 03:42:57,373
Rangers, Bruins.

4294
03:42:57,457 --> 03:43:00,873
Actually, is it cool
if I show Hannah around first?

4295
03:43:00,957 --> 03:43:02,665
Yeah, of course.

4296
03:43:02,748 --> 03:43:05,082
You don't have to ask permission.
This is your house, too.

4297
03:43:07,998 --> 03:43:08,957
Here, I'll give you the tour.

4298
03:43:09,040 --> 03:43:10,498
Cool.

4299
03:43:10,582 --> 03:43:11,457
[knock on door]

4300
03:43:11,540 --> 03:43:13,082
Thank you so much.
Thank you for coming.

4301
03:43:13,165 --> 03:43:14,790
Who is that now?

4302
03:43:16,040 --> 03:43:17,540
We come bearing alcohol.

4303
03:43:17,623 --> 03:43:21,415
And we got tiny little boxes of cereal
stolen from the dining hall.

4304
03:43:21,498 --> 03:43:23,373
Hey, look, Tuck. More people.

4305
03:43:23,457 --> 03:43:25,373
Hannah said orphans were welcome.

4306
03:43:25,457 --> 03:43:27,248
They are. They are, yes.

4307
03:43:27,332 --> 03:43:29,373
Uh, just grab a seat.

4308
03:43:29,457 --> 03:43:30,832
Jules will grab you a drink.

4309
03:43:32,207 --> 03:43:36,457
Yeah. Just make yourselves at home
here in the living room.

4310
03:43:36,540 --> 03:43:38,623
Okay, thank you, guys. Happy Thanksgiving.

4311
03:43:38,707 --> 03:43:40,207
[all] Happy Thanksgiving.

4312
03:43:44,498 --> 03:43:45,998
[stove beeps]

4313
03:43:46,082 --> 03:43:48,040
Why is the stuffing not in the oven yet?

4314
03:43:48,123 --> 03:43:51,123
Because the corn pudding and the green
bean casserole are already in there.

4315
03:43:51,207 --> 03:43:53,082
Here, please consult the oven schedule.

4316
03:43:54,082 --> 03:43:55,373
I did all the math.

4317
03:43:55,457 --> 03:43:58,373
The stuffing needs to hang out
in the neutral zone.

4318
03:43:58,457 --> 03:44:00,248
- It only takes 30 minutes.
- [stove beeps]

4319
03:44:00,332 --> 03:44:02,040
If you guys were half as good at hockey...

4320
03:44:02,123 --> 03:44:04,123
Jules, I can't right now.

4321
03:44:04,207 --> 03:44:05,123
Please.

4322
03:44:05,207 --> 03:44:06,748
- Go.
- Gravy. Guys, please.

4323
03:44:06,832 --> 03:44:08,498
- Somebody taste it. Thank you.
- Logan, try it.

4324
03:44:10,248 --> 03:44:13,665
And for the end of the tour, this is me.

4325
03:44:22,707 --> 03:44:23,665
You okay?

4326
03:44:24,623 --> 03:44:26,915
Yeah, yeah, it's just weird
being back here.

4327
03:44:26,998 --> 03:44:29,248
After my mom died,
I went off to boarding school,

4328
03:44:29,332 --> 03:44:31,707
and I never really lived here again.

4329
03:44:31,790 --> 03:44:33,873
Yeah, I can tell. [laughs]

4330
03:44:33,957 --> 03:44:36,707
Is your dad running
a storage business on the side?

4331
03:44:36,790 --> 03:44:38,082
[both chuckle]

4332
03:44:38,748 --> 03:44:41,373
This is just all the stuff he signs
when he goes to mall appearances

4333
03:44:41,457 --> 03:44:42,707
or conventions or whatever.

4334
03:44:42,790 --> 03:44:43,748
Right.

4335
03:44:44,373 --> 03:44:46,165
Trying to keep the legend alive.

4336
03:44:47,582 --> 03:44:49,582
His best years are behind him.

4337
03:44:52,123 --> 03:44:53,832
Are you afraid that'll happen to you?

4338
03:44:53,915 --> 03:44:57,040
This is what success
looks like, eventually.

4339
03:44:58,373 --> 03:45:00,248
Or I could tear my ACL tomorrow

4340
03:45:00,332 --> 03:45:04,498
and get stuck bagging groceries
at the Stop 'N' Shop.

4341
03:45:05,790 --> 03:45:08,207
Not that--
Not that there's anything wrong with that.

4342
03:45:08,290 --> 03:45:11,248
Hey, my mom works at Bob's Market, so...

4343
03:45:12,248 --> 03:45:15,207
Yeah, not-- Yeah, that wasn't really
a dream, either, so...

4344
03:45:16,540 --> 03:45:18,123
What was?

4345
03:45:18,207 --> 03:45:20,623
I don't know. She-- She was a singer.

4346
03:45:20,707 --> 03:45:23,040
Her high school choir
won a bunch of competitions,

4347
03:45:23,123 --> 03:45:25,082
but I don't know,
she never really went for it.

4348
03:45:25,165 --> 03:45:26,915
She must be proud of you, then.

4349
03:45:26,998 --> 03:45:29,540
Yeah, I just think
she wants me to be happy.

4350
03:45:31,207 --> 03:45:33,748
My dad, he's not really like that.

4351
03:45:33,832 --> 03:45:36,915
Or, I don't know about now, but he wasn't.

4352
03:45:36,998 --> 03:45:39,457
Not just with hockey, with everything.
He was always...

4353
03:45:40,790 --> 03:45:42,082
so...

4354
03:45:42,165 --> 03:45:43,540
Intense?

4355
03:45:43,623 --> 03:45:44,665
Yeah.

4356
03:45:44,748 --> 03:45:46,873
- Yeah.
- Yeah, seriously intense.

4357
03:45:56,040 --> 03:45:59,332
Yeah, I don't know,
it just seems kind of sad.

4358
03:45:59,415 --> 03:46:02,707
Like you wake up one morning
and can't play hockey anymore.

4359
03:46:02,790 --> 03:46:04,207
Would you miss it?

4360
03:46:04,290 --> 03:46:05,957
It's the only thing I'm good at.

4361
03:46:06,040 --> 03:46:08,373
That's not true. And that's not an answer.

4362
03:46:08,457 --> 03:46:09,790
[laughs]

4363
03:46:10,998 --> 03:46:12,415
I think I would be...

4364
03:46:13,790 --> 03:46:15,665
like, relieved.

4365
03:46:21,832 --> 03:46:23,082
[cell phone vibrates]

4366
03:46:23,165 --> 03:46:24,248
Sorry.

4367
03:46:25,790 --> 03:46:29,373
Uh, Allie said that they wanted
to wish me a Happy Thanksgiving.

4368
03:46:29,457 --> 03:46:30,707
Take it.

4369
03:46:30,790 --> 03:46:31,665
Are you sure?

4370
03:46:37,248 --> 03:46:38,665
Yeah, I've got this.

4371
03:46:39,998 --> 03:46:41,207
Okay.

4372
03:46:44,457 --> 03:46:45,332
Hey.

4373
03:46:45,415 --> 03:46:46,623
[laughing] Oh, my gosh!

4374
03:46:46,707 --> 03:46:48,248
Hi, everyone.

4375
03:46:51,332 --> 03:46:55,165
Okay, we have more people here
than a Walmart on a Black Friday.

4376
03:46:55,248 --> 03:46:57,832
We are going to loaves and fishes
this whole thing.

4377
03:46:57,915 --> 03:47:02,123
I'mma go get potatoes
from the extra fridge, and then, um...

4378
03:47:02,207 --> 03:47:04,082
- Pat-dry?
- ...pat-dry the bird, yes.

4379
03:47:04,165 --> 03:47:05,915
- Yes.
- Go get 'em, buddy.

4380
03:47:05,998 --> 03:47:08,707
Wait, wait, wait.
No marshmallows on the sweet potatoes?

4381
03:47:08,790 --> 03:47:10,457
[man] They're already sweet.

4382
03:47:10,540 --> 03:47:13,207
Okay, that's fucking blasphemy.
You're a blasphemer.

4383
03:47:13,290 --> 03:47:14,623
I will die on this hill.

4384
03:47:14,707 --> 03:47:16,957
We never had marshmallows
on our sweet potatoes.

4385
03:47:17,040 --> 03:47:19,707
- We never had sweet potatoes.
- I had a sweet potato taco one year.

4386
03:47:19,790 --> 03:47:22,123
Tacos? On Thanksgiving?

4387
03:47:22,207 --> 03:47:24,165
It's actually the best time
for tacos, honestly.

4388
03:47:24,665 --> 03:47:27,498
Especially when your big bro has a sweet
sponsorship deal with Taco Shack.

4389
03:47:27,582 --> 03:47:29,873
Ah. They're open on Thanksgiving?

4390
03:47:29,957 --> 03:47:32,248
Yeah, they're the only place
open on Thanksgiving.

4391
03:47:32,332 --> 03:47:35,540
And we learned that the hard way
when our mom got drunk one year

4392
03:47:35,623 --> 03:47:36,915
and forgot she was grilling chicken.

4393
03:47:36,998 --> 03:47:39,040
The propane tank almost leveled the block.

4394
03:47:39,123 --> 03:47:40,998
- Whoa.
- It was a blessing, actually.

4395
03:47:41,082 --> 03:47:43,498
Mama Logan was never known
for her cooking.

4396
03:47:44,748 --> 03:47:45,998
I know.

4397
03:47:46,498 --> 03:47:47,832
We should bring Mom Taco Shack.

4398
03:47:47,915 --> 03:47:49,373
Absolutely not.

4399
03:47:50,248 --> 03:47:51,873
Well, she's probably surrounded
by strangers

4400
03:47:51,957 --> 03:47:53,373
eating gross rehab food right now.

4401
03:47:54,290 --> 03:47:55,290
So?

4402
03:47:55,373 --> 03:47:57,498
So, she needs our support.

4403
03:47:57,582 --> 03:47:58,665
Should we be here for this?

4404
03:47:58,748 --> 03:48:01,873
I supported her the last time she went in,
and the time before that,

4405
03:48:01,957 --> 03:48:02,832
and the time before that.

4406
03:48:02,915 --> 03:48:04,832
It's Thanksgiving,
and she's fucking family, John.

4407
03:48:04,915 --> 03:48:06,540
She's in fucking rehab, Jules.

4408
03:48:06,623 --> 03:48:07,790
Exactly.

4409
03:48:08,873 --> 03:48:10,373
She's...

4410
03:48:10,457 --> 03:48:11,707
She's trying.

4411
03:48:11,790 --> 03:48:15,332
Okay, new plan.
I'm gonna whip up some spinach casserole.

4412
03:48:16,665 --> 03:48:17,707
What?

4413
03:48:18,207 --> 03:48:19,415
You know what? Forget it.

4414
03:48:19,915 --> 03:48:21,332
I'll go myself.

4415
03:48:26,457 --> 03:48:28,290
Tucker! My friend.

4416
03:48:28,373 --> 03:48:29,748
We are here.

4417
03:48:29,832 --> 03:48:31,832
Yes. Yes, you are.

4418
03:48:31,915 --> 03:48:33,373
I'm so sorry to be late.

4419
03:48:33,457 --> 03:48:34,332
Uh-huh.

4420
03:48:34,415 --> 03:48:36,332
- So, Yanis from Latvia.
- Hi.

4421
03:48:36,832 --> 03:48:39,582
- Uh, Cheryl from Philippines.
- Hi.

4422
03:48:39,665 --> 03:48:41,498
- You know Arjun?
- Mm-mm. Hi.

4423
03:48:41,582 --> 03:48:43,957
- And Karl Heinz.
- Hello! Karl Heinz.

4424
03:48:44,040 --> 03:48:45,082
[all laugh]

4425
03:48:45,165 --> 03:48:47,207
- [glass shatters]
- [Lexi] Sorry.

4426
03:48:48,040 --> 03:48:50,832
You know what, boys and girls?
I need space to work.

4427
03:48:50,915 --> 03:48:53,540
Everybody, we are going
to take this shindig outside.

4428
03:48:53,623 --> 03:48:55,748
Let's go. Outside. Outside, guys.

4429
03:48:55,832 --> 03:48:57,665
- Outside, guys.
- [man] Outside.

4430
03:48:57,748 --> 03:48:59,290
Thank you, guys.

4431
03:48:59,373 --> 03:49:01,290
- [indistinct chatter]
- Thank you, guys.

4432
03:49:03,540 --> 03:49:05,623
[exhales]

4433
03:49:05,707 --> 03:49:07,332
[TV announcer] <i>The Bruins started the day</i>

4434
03:49:07,415 --> 03:49:10,207
<i>three points clear
of fifth-place Philadelphia,</i>

4435
03:49:10,290 --> 03:49:12,457
<i>and fourth in the East.</i>

4436
03:49:12,540 --> 03:49:13,832
<i>The game is on.</i>

4437
03:49:15,748 --> 03:49:19,373
<i>It looked like the Bruins
are gonna get that puck out.</i>

4438
03:49:19,457 --> 03:49:21,873
I heard you stopped by
and saw a Bruins practice.

4439
03:49:21,957 --> 03:49:23,498
Yeah.

4440
03:49:23,582 --> 03:49:25,373
You get a chance to show off?

4441
03:49:25,873 --> 03:49:27,540
Yeah, a little bit.

4442
03:49:27,623 --> 03:49:28,873
Attaboy.

4443
03:49:33,290 --> 03:49:36,373
Cindy seems... nice.

4444
03:49:36,457 --> 03:49:37,415
She is.

4445
03:49:37,498 --> 03:49:38,998
Knows hockey, too.

4446
03:49:39,082 --> 03:49:41,248
Penguins fan, but we're working on that.

4447
03:49:41,332 --> 03:49:42,748
All right. Good.

4448
03:49:43,707 --> 03:49:45,415
- [cheering on TV]
- Mm!

4449
03:49:45,498 --> 03:49:47,040
- There you go.
- Fuckin' A.

4450
03:49:47,123 --> 03:49:48,290
There you go.

4451
03:49:48,373 --> 03:49:50,623
Bonneville is giving the Bruins trouble.

4452
03:49:50,707 --> 03:49:51,915
He's too fast for the D.

4453
03:49:51,998 --> 03:49:53,540
Yeah, but he's slow on the backtrack.

4454
03:49:53,623 --> 03:49:55,332
They've just got to get
the puck off him first.

4455
03:49:55,415 --> 03:49:59,957
Mm. I bet the Bruins would love having you
on the ice a year early, huh?

4456
03:50:00,040 --> 03:50:03,873
They don't need me yet.
Fontano's got a few seasons left in him.

4457
03:50:03,957 --> 03:50:06,332
Plus, I'm not ready yet.

4458
03:50:06,415 --> 03:50:07,623
I want to graduate.

4459
03:50:07,707 --> 03:50:10,207
[announcer] <i>We'll be right back
after this commercial break.</i>

4460
03:50:11,498 --> 03:50:13,707
That's a smart choice, Garrett.

4461
03:50:15,665 --> 03:50:18,790
Probably good to be a little bit older
before you go pro.

4462
03:50:19,665 --> 03:50:24,332
Eighteen was really young for me
to be thrown in the deep end.

4463
03:50:24,415 --> 03:50:26,498
You'll be better equipped
to handle the pressure.

4464
03:50:29,957 --> 03:50:31,623
[announcer]
<i>And we're back.</i>

4465
03:50:31,707 --> 03:50:34,748
<i>Face off won by Levy
and the Bruins set it up.</i>

4466
03:50:34,832 --> 03:50:37,248
<i>The Rangers' penalty killing
has been outstanding.</i>

4467
03:50:37,332 --> 03:50:40,290
<i>A huge factor in the game
against the Bruins today.</i>

4468
03:50:40,373 --> 03:50:41,665
Okay, are you alone now?

4469
03:50:41,748 --> 03:50:43,832
Can we talk about Aunt Kathy's
new British accent?

4470
03:50:43,915 --> 03:50:46,498
And she goes by Kiara now.

4471
03:50:46,582 --> 03:50:48,207
It's like a whole thing.

4472
03:50:48,290 --> 03:50:50,165
Wasn't she in London for, like, a week?

4473
03:50:50,248 --> 03:50:51,873
- [boisterous chatter]
- [cell phone vibrating]

4474
03:50:52,873 --> 03:50:54,832
<i>- Al?</i>
- Huh?

4475
03:50:54,915 --> 03:50:57,040
<i>Um, no, yeah, totally.</i>

4476
03:50:57,123 --> 03:51:00,123
Uh, okay, what-- What's going on?

4477
03:51:00,207 --> 03:51:02,832
<i>Nothing, it's just like everyone's over.</i>

4478
03:51:02,915 --> 03:51:04,498
Hey, if you're busy, I...

4479
03:51:04,582 --> 03:51:07,373
Hey, Allie Hayes, I can hear your nails.
Who are you texting?

4480
03:51:07,457 --> 03:51:09,332
What? Nobody.

4481
03:51:09,415 --> 03:51:10,665
It's Sean.

4482
03:51:10,748 --> 03:51:12,707
- You're backsliding.
- Am not.

4483
03:51:13,623 --> 03:51:15,123
Hey, it's okay.

4484
03:51:15,207 --> 03:51:16,290
[laughs]

4485
03:51:16,373 --> 03:51:17,832
It's my dad. He, uh...

4486
03:51:18,832 --> 03:51:20,790
He can't find the remote again. He--

4487
03:51:20,873 --> 03:51:23,790
I swear he has ADHD,
but his generation's undiagnosable.

4488
03:51:24,998 --> 03:51:26,290
Oh, okay.

4489
03:51:27,290 --> 03:51:29,290
Hey, I should probably go help.

4490
03:51:29,373 --> 03:51:31,457
Um, love you, miss you. Gobble, gobble.

4491
03:51:31,540 --> 03:51:32,915
- [call disconnects]
- Oh...

4492
03:51:39,248 --> 03:51:40,623
[sighs]

4493
03:51:57,415 --> 03:51:58,665
[chuckles]

4494
03:52:40,665 --> 03:52:41,957
Happy Thanksgiving.

4495
03:52:42,040 --> 03:52:43,623
- You have an appointment?
- Hi.

4496
03:52:43,707 --> 03:52:45,748
No, I'm-- I'm here for Jean Logan.

4497
03:52:45,832 --> 03:52:47,290
And when did she check in?

4498
03:52:47,373 --> 03:52:48,457
Last week.

4499
03:52:48,540 --> 03:52:51,748
I'm sorry, new intakes
don't have visitation privileges yet.

4500
03:52:51,832 --> 03:52:54,123
No, I, uh... I have a delivery.

4501
03:52:55,082 --> 03:52:57,165
Can you just tell her it's from Jules?

4502
03:52:57,748 --> 03:52:58,790
[Logan] And John.

4503
03:53:02,123 --> 03:53:03,248
Excuse me?

4504
03:53:03,332 --> 03:53:05,665
I paid for this with my hard-earned cash.

4505
03:53:05,748 --> 03:53:06,873
Well, I'll Venmo you.

4506
03:53:06,957 --> 03:53:08,790
Jules and John, thank you.

4507
03:53:08,873 --> 03:53:12,373
[receptionist] Any particular message?
"Happy Thanksgiving," or...

4508
03:53:12,457 --> 03:53:14,873
Actually, uh, contraband, please.

4509
03:53:26,040 --> 03:53:27,540
It's a family tradition.

4510
03:53:28,790 --> 03:53:29,832
She'll get it.

4511
03:53:32,332 --> 03:53:33,873
Thank you.

4512
03:53:33,957 --> 03:53:35,332
It'll mean a lot to her.

4513
03:53:35,873 --> 03:53:38,082
Well, I'm here
because it means a lot to you.

4514
03:53:38,623 --> 03:53:39,957
And you're right.

4515
03:53:41,207 --> 03:53:42,623
She is trying.

4516
03:53:49,082 --> 03:53:52,748
So, what do you say we hit
the hardware store on the way back?

4517
03:53:52,832 --> 03:53:53,957
For real?

4518
03:53:54,040 --> 03:53:55,873
I mean, we gotta shore up our supplies

4519
03:53:55,957 --> 03:53:58,290
if we're gonna spread
the Logan love this holiday season.

4520
03:53:58,373 --> 03:54:01,873
In that case, we'd better hit
the Stop 'N' Shop, too.

4521
03:54:01,957 --> 03:54:04,748
One bag of marshmallows
ain't gonna cut it.

4522
03:54:04,832 --> 03:54:07,957
- [snaps fingers]
- Let's go. Come on.

4523
03:54:08,040 --> 03:54:08,915
[timers beeping]

4524
03:54:08,998 --> 03:54:12,415
<i>♪I'm your leader, I'm your teacher
I'm your Michelin Man...♪</i>

4525
03:54:12,498 --> 03:54:14,832
- Status check.
- All sides in the oven. Chef.

4526
03:54:14,915 --> 03:54:16,290
T-minus one hour. Chef.

4527
03:54:16,373 --> 03:54:18,165
- I've always wanted to say that.
- We crushed it.

4528
03:54:18,248 --> 03:54:22,457
Which means, <i>mis amigos,</i>
it is time to deep-fry the turkey!

4529
03:54:22,540 --> 03:54:24,540
[all cheer]

4530
03:54:25,040 --> 03:54:27,207
- Simms, you ready?
- Let's fucking do this.

4531
03:54:27,290 --> 03:54:29,665
[all] Ten, nine, eight,

4532
03:54:29,748 --> 03:54:32,665
seven, six, five,

4533
03:54:32,748 --> 03:54:36,915
four, three, two,

4534
03:54:36,998 --> 03:54:38,540
one!

4535
03:54:38,623 --> 03:54:41,040
Wait, I forgot to pat-dry the bird!

4536
03:54:41,123 --> 03:54:42,165
Oh!

4537
03:54:42,248 --> 03:54:44,207
["National Treasure"
by Barns Courtney playing]

4538
03:55:05,290 --> 03:55:08,207
- [man] Bonfire party!
- [cheering]

4539
03:55:10,748 --> 03:55:12,748
[mellow dinner music playing]

4540
03:55:12,832 --> 03:55:14,957
You guys are in for quite a treat.

4541
03:55:15,040 --> 03:55:17,832
Cindy's mashed potatoes
are really something.

4542
03:55:17,915 --> 03:55:19,290
And dairy-free.

4543
03:55:19,373 --> 03:55:20,915
It's a happy accident, Hannah.

4544
03:55:22,790 --> 03:55:25,582
I asked Cindy to, uh,

4545
03:55:25,665 --> 03:55:27,415
make the mac and cheese...

4546
03:55:28,082 --> 03:55:30,415
- With the breadcrumbs, uh-huh.
- With the breadcrumbs.

4547
03:55:30,498 --> 03:55:32,248
- Like Mom used to make.
- [Phil] Mm-hmm.

4548
03:55:32,832 --> 03:55:34,165
I didn't want to overstep.

4549
03:55:34,248 --> 03:55:35,998
[Garrett] No.

4550
03:55:36,082 --> 03:55:38,540
No, that's-- that's very kind. Thank you.

4551
03:55:38,623 --> 03:55:39,915
[Phil] Thanks for coming.

4552
03:55:41,498 --> 03:55:42,957
It means a lot to me.

4553
03:55:47,332 --> 03:55:49,165
Phil, would you?

4554
03:55:49,248 --> 03:55:50,540
Yes, of course.

4555
03:55:50,623 --> 03:55:52,832
We should say a little grace
before we dig in.

4556
03:55:53,832 --> 03:55:55,582
Oh.

4557
03:55:55,665 --> 03:55:56,832
Yeah.

4558
03:55:59,665 --> 03:56:04,790
Lord, thank you for this wonderful bounty
you have bestowed upon us.

4559
03:56:05,790 --> 03:56:09,832
Thank you for bringing us all together
to enjoy this delicious meal.

4560
03:56:09,915 --> 03:56:11,873
And for the hands that prepared it.

4561
03:56:13,248 --> 03:56:15,873
We ask you to guide us

4562
03:56:15,957 --> 03:56:19,373
towards love and understanding.

4563
03:56:22,790 --> 03:56:26,832
[voice becoming muffled] To experience
what it means to be family.

4564
03:56:30,582 --> 03:56:33,248
<i>In this life and the next.</i>

4565
03:56:33,332 --> 03:56:34,415
[angry shouting]

4566
03:56:34,498 --> 03:56:35,873
<i>Thank you, Lord.</i>

4567
03:56:36,915 --> 03:56:38,915
[muffled thuds]

4568
03:56:40,915 --> 03:56:42,248
[normal audio resumes] Amen.

4569
03:56:44,665 --> 03:56:45,957
Amen.

4570
03:56:59,748 --> 03:57:01,498
Everything okay?

4571
03:57:01,582 --> 03:57:02,457
[Cindy] Yeah.

4572
03:57:02,540 --> 03:57:04,040
I just got a chill.

4573
03:57:04,123 --> 03:57:05,832
She's thin-skinned, this one.

4574
03:57:05,915 --> 03:57:08,540
Not built for Boston winter.

4575
03:57:08,623 --> 03:57:12,040
Why don't you go upstairs
and get a different sweater, darling?

4576
03:57:15,040 --> 03:57:16,248
No! Don't!

4577
03:57:16,332 --> 03:57:18,915
- Whoa!
- Just sit.

4578
03:57:20,457 --> 03:57:22,123
Is there a problem?

4579
03:57:23,165 --> 03:57:24,415
Sorry, I just...

4580
03:57:26,582 --> 03:57:27,957
I need a...

4581
03:57:28,040 --> 03:57:29,082
Um...

4582
03:57:29,165 --> 03:57:30,540
I'm so sorry.

4583
03:57:30,623 --> 03:57:32,623
I'm not feeling well.

4584
03:57:36,540 --> 03:57:37,582
Can we go?

4585
03:57:41,165 --> 03:57:42,373
Let's go.

4586
03:57:44,707 --> 03:57:46,665
- [breathing heavily]
- Slow down.

4587
03:57:47,332 --> 03:57:49,373
- Garrett, give me the keys. I'm driving.
- Hannah.

4588
03:57:49,457 --> 03:57:50,498
Garrett.

4589
03:57:51,707 --> 03:57:53,207
Please.

4590
03:57:54,582 --> 03:57:57,165
Wait! Your coats!

4591
03:57:59,123 --> 03:58:00,207
Thank you.

4592
03:58:01,790 --> 03:58:03,748
I'm gonna go warm up the car.

4593
03:58:09,165 --> 03:58:10,207
Your wrist.

4594
03:58:10,290 --> 03:58:11,665
It was an accident.

4595
03:58:11,748 --> 03:58:12,998
No, it wasn't.

4596
03:58:13,665 --> 03:58:15,332
I'm sorry I ruined Thanksgiving.

4597
03:58:15,415 --> 03:58:17,165
Your father really wanted us all to...

4598
03:58:17,248 --> 03:58:19,540
No, you-you-you didn't ruin...

4599
03:58:21,873 --> 03:58:24,123
You can't stay with him.

4600
03:58:24,207 --> 03:58:26,623
Look, he felt awful after.

4601
03:58:26,707 --> 03:58:28,082
And it's just...

4602
03:58:28,165 --> 03:58:30,707
- It's not who he is.
- It's exactly who he is.

4603
03:58:30,790 --> 03:58:33,415
He says it's not
gonna happen again, right?

4604
03:58:33,498 --> 03:58:36,582
He makes promises. He says he'll change.
It's a lie. It's all a fucking lie.

4605
03:58:36,665 --> 03:58:38,498
He doesn't care about you.
He doesn't care about me.

4606
03:58:38,582 --> 03:58:40,248
All he cares about is Phil fucking Graham.
That's it.

4607
03:58:40,332 --> 03:58:42,082
Listen to me.

4608
03:58:42,165 --> 03:58:44,332
My mom didn't have the chance to get out.

4609
03:58:44,415 --> 03:58:45,790
But you do.

4610
03:58:47,540 --> 03:58:48,873
Please leave.

4611
03:58:48,957 --> 03:58:50,082
Please.

4612
03:59:02,707 --> 03:59:04,373
It's complicated.

4613
03:59:06,873 --> 03:59:07,790
[sighs]

4614
03:59:07,873 --> 03:59:09,873
["Over and Over Again"
by Matthew Perryman Jones playing]

4615
03:59:16,873 --> 03:59:18,123
- [door closes]
- [sighs]

4616
03:59:19,165 --> 03:59:22,998
<i>♪I can see you in myself ♪</i>

4617
03:59:23,082 --> 03:59:26,707
<i>♪And it's scaring me to death ♪</i>

4618
03:59:27,707 --> 03:59:30,998
<i>♪You're running from what was ♪</i>

4619
03:59:31,082 --> 03:59:34,040
<i>♪And what hasn't happened yet ♪</i>

4620
03:59:35,207 --> 03:59:38,207
<i>♪I can't be someone else ♪</i>

4621
03:59:38,290 --> 03:59:42,332
