- I wasn't...
- Yeah, you were.

5807
04:59:20,223 --> 04:59:21,973
You really can't be alone, can you?

5808
04:59:22,057 --> 04:59:24,640
No, Sean. It wasn't like that, I swear.

5809
04:59:25,390 --> 04:59:26,807
Oh, come on. Sean!

5810
04:59:30,265 --> 04:59:32,598
- Night, guys. Good luck tomorrow.
- Thanks.

5811
04:59:32,682 --> 04:59:35,015
Yeah, if you're on the ice with Delaney,
you just gotta do what G says.

5812
04:59:35,098 --> 04:59:36,432
He can't hold up against all the pressure.

5813
04:59:36,515 --> 04:59:37,765
Who?

5814
04:59:37,848 --> 04:59:39,807
St. A's new center, Aaron Delaney.

5815
04:59:39,890 --> 04:59:41,557
Dude's a beast.

5816
04:59:56,432 --> 05:00:00,557
[heartbeat thumping]

5817
05:00:07,848 --> 05:00:08,932
[Hannah gasps]

5818
05:00:09,807 --> 05:00:11,348
[breathing heavily]

5819
05:00:12,223 --> 05:00:16,890
<i>♪I've been numb, I'm dying to feel ♪</i>

5820
05:00:16,973 --> 05:00:21,473
<i>♪Touching a grave that isn't real ♪</i>

5821
05:00:21,557 --> 05:00:25,765
<i>♪Touching a ghost that I can't see ♪</i>

5822
05:00:25,848 --> 05:00:29,932
<i>♪But the ghost is me ♪</i>

5823
05:00:30,015 --> 05:00:31,515
[echo of crowd cheering]

5824
05:00:31,598 --> 05:00:35,515
<i>♪A melting candle on a piece of cake ♪</i>

5825
05:00:36,140 --> 05:00:40,682
<i>♪I can't tell if I'm awake ♪</i>

5826
05:00:40,765 --> 05:00:44,848
<i>♪There is a ghost that stares at me ♪</i>

5827
05:00:44,932 --> 05:00:49,307
<i>♪But the ghost is me ♪</i>

5828
05:00:50,015 --> 05:00:54,098
<i>♪The ghost is me ♪</i>

5829
05:01:04,848 --> 05:01:06,973
<i>♪Fall through the floor ♪</i>

5830
05:01:07,057 --> 05:01:09,557
<i>♪Walk through walls ♪</i>

5831
05:01:09,640 --> 05:01:14,182
<i>♪Looking at pictures in the hall ♪</i>

5832
05:01:14,265 --> 05:01:18,515
<i>♪Staring in mirrors so I can see ♪</i>

5833
05:01:18,598 --> 05:01:21,557
<i>♪That the ghost is me ♪</i>

5834
05:01:21,640 --> 05:01:22,932
[breathing heavily]

5835
05:01:23,973 --> 05:01:28,765
<i>♪Showing up when you least expect ♪</i>

5836
05:01:28,848 --> 05:01:33,265
<i>♪A little girl that died in a wreck ♪</i>

5837
05:01:33,348 --> 05:01:38,057
<i>♪Alive again and finally free ♪</i>

5838
05:01:38,140 --> 05:01:42,265
<i>♪The ghost is me ♪</i>

5839
05:01:42,890 --> 05:01:47,098
<i>♪The ghost is me ♪</i>

5840
05:01:47,848 --> 05:01:49,182
[exhales]

5841
05:01:49,265 --> 05:01:52,182
<i>♪The ghost is me ♪</i>

5842
05:01:53,140 --> 05:01:55,973
[song instrumentals continue]

5843
05:03:38,765 --> 05:03:41,973
[song fades out]

5844
05:05:58,363 --> 05:05:59,488
[crowd cheering]

5845
05:05:59,571 --> 05:06:02,030
[announcer] <i>Delaney with the puck!
He's trying to fend them off!</i>

5846
05:06:02,113 --> 05:06:03,321
<i>Delaney shoots!</i>

5847
05:06:03,405 --> 05:06:04,863
<i>He scores!</i>

5848
05:06:04,946 --> 05:06:06,821
<i>Ransom wins!</i>

5849
05:06:06,905 --> 05:06:09,155
<i>Ransom wins!</i>

5850
05:06:09,238 --> 05:06:11,071
[cheers and applause]

5851
05:06:12,155 --> 05:06:14,738
Hannah. Hannah.

5852
05:06:15,738 --> 05:06:16,905
We won.

5853
05:06:18,696 --> 05:06:20,363
[band playing percussive music]

5854
05:06:24,988 --> 05:06:26,905
["This Too Shall Pass" by OK Go playing]

5855
05:06:29,113 --> 05:06:31,571
<i>♪When the morning comes...♪</i>

5856
05:06:32,113 --> 05:06:34,446
Uh, excuse me, gentlemen.

5857
05:06:34,530 --> 05:06:37,280
The UN has declared
an international band emergency,

5858
05:06:37,363 --> 05:06:40,071
and they say that my dad
is the only man for the job.

5859
05:06:40,155 --> 05:06:41,655
An international band emergency?

5860
05:06:41,738 --> 05:06:42,946
Have they called Prince?

5861
05:06:43,030 --> 05:06:44,988
They tried, but he is famously dead.

5862
05:06:45,071 --> 05:06:47,655
Good God, this is worse than I thought.

5863
05:06:47,738 --> 05:06:49,321
- Sorry, guys.
- [Hannah laughs]

5864
05:06:49,405 --> 05:06:51,071
You're so weird.

5865
05:06:51,155 --> 05:06:53,821
Also, can we hit Dairy Queen
on the way home?

5866
05:06:53,905 --> 05:06:57,696
What? Are you saying the international
band emergency was a ruse?

5867
05:06:57,780 --> 05:06:59,405
Is Prince even dead?

5868
05:06:59,488 --> 05:07:03,280
Han! Honey, you were phenomenal.

5869
05:07:03,363 --> 05:07:05,613
Uh, how was I?

5870
05:07:05,696 --> 05:07:07,696
Mm, you were okay, too.

5871
05:07:07,780 --> 05:07:08,905
Ah, yes!

5872
05:07:08,988 --> 05:07:10,488
[laughs]

5873
05:07:10,571 --> 05:07:11,988
Okay, can I help you?

5874
05:07:12,071 --> 05:07:15,155
[Greg] I just want to know
how your new song is coming along.

5875
05:07:15,238 --> 05:07:16,655
[breathing heavily]

5876
05:07:16,738 --> 05:07:19,530
It must be going well,
because you missed three cues tonight.

5877
05:07:19,613 --> 05:07:21,071
The muse waits for no one.

5878
05:07:21,155 --> 05:07:22,655
[Greg]
<i>Oh, does the muse play clarinet?</i>

5879
05:07:23,030 --> 05:07:25,780
Because we're looking
for a new alternate first chair.

5880
05:07:27,738 --> 05:07:29,571
[panting]

5881
05:07:30,655 --> 05:07:31,696
[woman] <i>Just write, Hannah.</i>

5882
05:07:32,030 --> 05:07:34,030
[breathing heavily]

5883
05:07:38,530 --> 05:07:40,071
["This Too Shall Pass" playing
over headphones]

5884
05:07:40,155 --> 05:07:41,405
- [knock on door]
- [Allie] Han?

5885
05:07:41,488 --> 05:07:43,196
I'm gonna skip the game today.

5886
05:07:43,280 --> 05:07:45,738
Got an extra monster cookie
if you want one.

5887
05:07:45,821 --> 05:07:47,113
[knocking]

5888
05:07:47,196 --> 05:07:48,655
Hannah?

5889
05:07:48,738 --> 05:07:50,030
Babe, you okay?

5890
05:07:50,113 --> 05:07:51,530
[music stops]

5891
05:07:51,613 --> 05:07:53,571
Yeah, yeah, sorry, I'm...

5892
05:07:55,071 --> 05:07:56,321
I'm not super hungry.

5893
05:07:56,405 --> 05:07:58,446
Uh, don't worry about me, I'm-- I'm good.

5894
05:07:59,488 --> 05:08:00,905
[Allie] Okay, love you.

5895
05:08:00,988 --> 05:08:03,113
[dramatic music playing]

5896
05:08:06,613 --> 05:08:09,571
- [breathing heavily]
- [heart pounding]

5897
05:08:14,113 --> 05:08:15,238
[breathes sharply]

5898
05:08:22,696 --> 05:08:24,988
[Dean]
Look at those smug motherfuckers.

5899
05:08:25,071 --> 05:08:27,405
Their ten-game streak ends now.

5900
05:08:27,488 --> 05:08:29,946
[exhales] Not if their new center
has anything to say about it.

5901
05:08:30,030 --> 05:08:32,405
[Dean] Please, he's been skating
in fucking cornfields.

5902
05:08:32,488 --> 05:08:34,113
- Iowa, or whatever.
- [Birdie] Indiana.

5903
05:08:34,196 --> 05:08:36,071
Kid's fast as fuck. Physical, too.

5904
05:08:36,155 --> 05:08:37,780
Doesn't matter. Nothing's getting past us.

5905
05:08:38,571 --> 05:08:40,321
[speaking Czech]

5906
05:08:40,405 --> 05:08:41,696
[Dean] Yeah, see? Simms gets it.

5907
05:08:41,780 --> 05:08:43,613
Yeah, come on, boys.
Let's get it.

5908
05:08:43,696 --> 05:08:45,863
Fuck, yeah. Let's go.

5909
05:08:48,946 --> 05:08:49,821
[door closes]

5910
05:08:49,905 --> 05:08:53,196
He also doesn't back down from anything.
Same as Garrett.

5911
05:08:53,280 --> 05:08:55,905
Oh, shit. Papa Graham's mad early.

5912
05:08:55,988 --> 05:08:57,446
No pressure, man.

5913
05:09:06,321 --> 05:09:08,613
Garrett, good to see you.

5914
05:09:09,655 --> 05:09:10,946
[sighs]

5915
05:09:13,655 --> 05:09:15,738
Looks like you got
a tough one out there today.

5916
05:09:15,821 --> 05:09:17,155
- Feeling good?
- [door opens]

5917
05:09:17,238 --> 05:09:19,446
Yeah, you know what?
Don't worry about me. I'm ready.

5918
05:09:19,530 --> 05:09:21,363
Sorry, I left my phone in the car.

5919
05:09:21,446 --> 05:09:22,696
It's okay.

5920
05:09:22,780 --> 05:09:23,863
Hi, Garrett.

5921
05:09:27,030 --> 05:09:28,113
[gasps]

5922
05:09:29,571 --> 05:09:30,821
Cindy.

5923
05:09:30,905 --> 05:09:32,238
Good luck out there today.

5924
05:09:35,571 --> 05:09:37,113
Yeah.

5925
05:09:37,196 --> 05:09:38,405
Thanks.

5926
05:09:50,738 --> 05:09:52,738
[dramatic music playing]

5927
05:09:55,905 --> 05:09:57,613
[cell phone vibrates]

5928
05:10:05,738 --> 05:10:07,405
[vibrating continues]

5929
05:10:08,738 --> 05:10:09,988
[breathes sharply]

5930
05:10:13,071 --> 05:10:15,863
[Allie] Sean, I am so sorry
that you had to find out like that.

5931
05:10:15,946 --> 05:10:17,988
I never meant to hurt your feelings.

5932
05:10:18,071 --> 05:10:21,113
But also, literally, how dare you suggest
that I am incapable of being alone?

5933
05:10:21,196 --> 05:10:24,405
Like, that's so fucked of you,
Sean. So fucked.

5934
05:10:24,488 --> 05:10:26,030
Again, could not be more sorry.

5935
05:10:26,113 --> 05:10:29,071
- Please just call me back or text me or--
- [voicemail beeps]

5936
05:10:29,155 --> 05:10:32,071
[computerized voice]
<i>Please hang up or press one to re-record.</i>

5937
05:10:35,780 --> 05:10:37,696
- Oh.
- Allie, what are you doing here?

5938
05:10:37,780 --> 05:10:39,363
Uh, this is the drama building.

5939
05:10:39,446 --> 05:10:41,863
I'm in the correct place.
What are you doing here?

5940
05:10:41,946 --> 05:10:44,571
This is perfect. You're not busy, right?
I need a huge favor.

5941
05:10:44,655 --> 05:10:47,946
No, Beau, sorry, I can't
take on anyone else's stress today.

5942
05:10:48,030 --> 05:10:49,946
I am emotionally raw.
I'm the shell of a woman.

5943
05:10:50,030 --> 05:10:52,196
Okay. Okay. Thank you, Ira.

5944
05:10:53,863 --> 05:10:54,863
You, too, Ira.

5945
05:10:56,071 --> 05:10:57,238
Bye, Ira.

5946
05:10:57,780 --> 05:11:01,238
Sorry about that.
Ira is not great at ending conversations.

5947
05:11:01,321 --> 05:11:02,863
Jo, this is Allie. Allie--

5948
05:11:02,946 --> 05:11:04,113
You're Joanna Maxwell.

5949
05:11:04,196 --> 05:11:05,280
Yeah, Allie's a fan.

5950
05:11:06,071 --> 05:11:07,405
Nice to meet you.

5951
05:11:07,488 --> 05:11:11,280
Wait, are you Allie Hayes?
Don't we have the same agent?

5952
05:11:11,946 --> 05:11:13,238
You know who I am.

5953
05:11:14,530 --> 05:11:16,113
Joanna Maxwell knows who I am.

5954
05:11:16,196 --> 05:11:17,196
Well, you can just call me Jo.

5955
05:11:17,280 --> 05:11:20,280
Yo, respectfully, there is literally
no way I can make that happen.

5956
05:11:20,363 --> 05:11:22,155
- [chuckles]
- Joanna's back here doing a master class

5957
05:11:22,238 --> 05:11:24,113
with the seniors,
because she's so famous.

5958
05:11:24,196 --> 05:11:25,571
Definitely not famous.

5959
05:11:25,655 --> 05:11:28,363
And because she's so famous,
she has this big self-tape.

5960
05:11:28,446 --> 05:11:30,613
- It's a same-day audition.
- Last time I read with Jo,

5961
05:11:30,696 --> 05:11:31,655
I got in trouble
for my voice

5962
05:11:31,738 --> 05:11:33,946
- being "stiff and distracting."
- Well...

5963
05:11:34,030 --> 05:11:36,488
So, I thought that maybe
you could read with her, Allie,

5964
05:11:36,571 --> 05:11:39,405
so I could go do literally anything else.

5965
05:11:39,488 --> 05:11:40,613
- [scoffs]
- What?

5966
05:11:40,696 --> 05:11:41,655
- Beau...
- Uh-huh?

5967
05:11:41,738 --> 05:11:43,363
You don't just ask someone
to be your reader.

5968
05:11:43,446 --> 05:11:45,280
- There's an etiquette, fool.
- Mm-hmm.

5969
05:11:45,363 --> 05:11:47,488
Sorry about him.
I couldn't ask you to do that.

5970
05:11:47,571 --> 05:11:48,821
It would derail your entire day.

5971
05:11:48,905 --> 05:11:52,488
No, no, no, derail it, please.
Seriously, it is not a problem.

5972
05:11:52,571 --> 05:11:56,696
I would be honored
to read with <i>the</i> Joanna Maxwell.

5973
05:12:00,821 --> 05:12:02,113
- [whistle blows]
- This is it, folks.

5974
05:12:02,196 --> 05:12:04,488
The start of our
long-awaited game with St. A's

5975
05:12:04,571 --> 05:12:06,321
and their new center, Aaron Delaney.

5976
05:12:06,405 --> 05:12:08,488
[rock music playing]

5977
05:12:10,988 --> 05:12:12,655
[Jules]
And we're underway here in the first.

5978
05:12:12,738 --> 05:12:14,446
Hawks take possession.

5979
05:12:15,488 --> 05:12:16,738
[grunts]

5980
05:12:16,821 --> 05:12:18,155
- [crowd groans]
- [Jules] Oh, shit.

5981
05:12:18,238 --> 05:12:19,780
Brutal hit from Aaron Delaney.

5982
05:12:19,863 --> 05:12:24,488
Seems the new guy's fitting right in with
St. A's legendary trash-talking bullies.

5983
05:12:24,571 --> 05:12:25,696
- [grunts]
- [crowd groans]

5984
05:12:27,363 --> 05:12:29,863
- [groans]
- Whoa! How is that not a penalty?

5985
05:12:29,946 --> 05:12:31,488
Hawks regain possession.

5986
05:12:32,155 --> 05:12:34,446
Graham starts out
from behind his own net and...

5987
05:12:34,530 --> 05:12:36,988
- Oh! Delaney says, nope.
- [crowd groans]

5988
05:12:37,571 --> 05:12:39,196
[Jules]
He shoots... and beats

5989
05:12:39,280 --> 05:12:41,238
Simms's blocker side
for the goal.

5990
05:12:41,321 --> 05:12:42,280
[crowd jeering]

5991
05:12:42,363 --> 05:12:44,613
Come on, Graham.
It's not fun if you don't fight back.

5992
05:12:44,696 --> 05:12:45,946
Fuck you.

5993
05:12:46,030 --> 05:12:48,238
[laughs]
Take it easy, princess.

5994
05:12:49,113 --> 05:12:50,363
Whoo!

5995
05:12:50,446 --> 05:12:52,446
Hey, come on, bro.

5996
05:12:52,530 --> 05:12:54,905
- Shake it off. You got this.
- [crowd audio fades and distorts]

5997
05:12:55,696 --> 05:12:57,321
[Garrett]
<i>Wellsy, where are you?</i>

5998
05:13:14,613 --> 05:13:16,905
- [breathing heavily]
- [woman] Just write, Hannah.

5999
05:13:39,446 --> 05:13:40,571
[vibrating]

6000
05:13:41,655 --> 05:13:43,655
[ominous music playing]

6001
05:13:46,280 --> 05:13:47,946
[breathing heavily]

6002
05:13:48,988 --> 05:13:52,030
- [sniffling, gasping]
- [vibrating continues]

6003
05:13:52,113 --> 05:13:54,488
- [stick hit echoes]
- [Jules] <i>Nasty cross-check by Delaney.</i>

6004
05:13:54,571 --> 05:13:56,905
<i>Vipers are absolutely dominating
the Hawks right now.</i>

6005
05:13:56,988 --> 05:13:59,321
<i>Hawks can't play the zone.
Vipers collect the puck</i>

6006
05:13:59,405 --> 05:14:00,780
<i>in the Hawks' zone.
Are you kidding?</i>

6007
05:14:00,863 --> 05:14:01,988
<i>The Vipers are relentless.</i>

6008
05:14:02,071 --> 05:14:04,738
<i>There's is a slashing penalty
on St. A's 29.</i>

6009
05:14:04,821 --> 05:14:06,738
- [woman] Just write, Hannah.
- <i>There's Delaney again.</i>

6010
05:14:06,821 --> 05:14:08,655
<i>What the actual fuck?</i>

6011
05:14:08,738 --> 05:14:10,155
<i>Delaney shoots.</i>

6012
05:14:10,238 --> 05:14:11,405
[breathing heavily]

6013
05:14:15,280 --> 05:14:17,738
[Jensen] Well, that wasn't
the first period I was looking for.

6014
05:14:17,821 --> 05:14:19,655
Graham, Delaney's shadowing you.

6015
05:14:19,738 --> 05:14:21,696
Move the puck. Look at Birdie and Dean.

6016
05:14:21,780 --> 05:14:24,113
We got two periods left.
Your turnovers are killing us.

6017
05:14:24,196 --> 05:14:26,113
- Don't worry about us. We're good.
- [imitates buzzer]

6018
05:14:26,196 --> 05:14:28,155
Fuck that. I'm not good.

6019
05:14:28,238 --> 05:14:30,863
[Jensen] Let's just work as a team
and try not to do it all ourselves.

6020
05:14:30,946 --> 05:14:33,655
- No more one-on-one sloppiness.
- I got it, okay? Fine.

6021
05:14:33,738 --> 05:14:36,321
Hey, cut the attitude, Graham.

6022
05:14:36,405 --> 05:14:37,488
I mean it.

6023
05:14:41,196 --> 05:14:43,196
Hey, Delaney's trying
to take you out of the game,

6024
05:14:43,280 --> 05:14:45,488
so take their defenders out, too.
As soon as the puck comes in,

6025
05:14:45,571 --> 05:14:48,071
- you just get rid of it.
- Who died and made you coach?

6026
05:14:48,155 --> 05:14:49,738
I'm out there, too, man.

6027
05:14:49,821 --> 05:14:51,905
Okay, then worry about yourself,
all right?

6028
05:14:51,988 --> 05:14:53,696
Okay, fine.

6029
05:14:54,780 --> 05:14:56,613
I don't know what your problem is,

6030
05:14:56,696 --> 05:14:59,738
but I suggest you do
whatever it takes to work it out.

6031
05:14:59,821 --> 05:15:01,155
Fucking quick.

6032
05:15:06,905 --> 05:15:08,571
[exhales heavily]

6033
05:15:12,363 --> 05:15:13,780
[exhales]

6034
05:15:17,321 --> 05:15:18,946
[phone line rings]

6035
05:15:23,738 --> 05:15:25,155
[cell phone vibrating]

6036
05:15:35,113 --> 05:15:37,113
[soft piano playing]

6037
05:15:46,738 --> 05:15:48,738
[piano volume increases]

6038
05:16:55,988 --> 05:16:56,988
[gasps]

6039
05:17:04,905 --> 05:17:06,780
Sorry. Sorry. Uh...

6040
05:17:06,863 --> 05:17:09,655
I-I couldn't be in my room, so I came.

6041
05:17:09,738 --> 05:17:11,113
And I-I heard.

6042
05:17:13,488 --> 05:17:15,488
Who was that you were playing?

6043
05:17:16,155 --> 05:17:18,030
It's actually an original.

6044
05:17:18,113 --> 05:17:22,571
Part of a series I wrote
when my son first went off to day care.

6045
05:17:22,655 --> 05:17:23,780
[chuckles]

6046
05:17:23,863 --> 05:17:26,613
Kind of exploring the emptiness of time.

6047
05:17:26,696 --> 05:17:27,946
Wow. Y--

6048
05:17:29,571 --> 05:17:31,280
- You're incredible.
- Ah.

6049
05:17:31,363 --> 05:17:32,571
I would hope so.

6050
05:17:32,655 --> 05:17:34,655
- [plays notes]
- That's why I'm here, right?

6051
05:17:38,571 --> 05:17:39,571
You okay?

6052
05:17:40,905 --> 05:17:42,530
Yeah, I finally get it.

6053
05:17:43,238 --> 05:17:45,738
When you said,
"Write music that lets people in."

6054
05:17:45,821 --> 05:17:50,071
Like, just now, I-I didn't know
it was about your son, but I felt it.

6055
05:17:52,363 --> 05:17:54,238
That's a sweet compliment.

6056
05:17:55,030 --> 05:17:58,071
Just having a hard time taking it,

6057
05:17:58,155 --> 05:18:01,405
because of the general melancholy.

6058
05:18:02,655 --> 05:18:04,363
Uh, it's...

6059
05:18:04,446 --> 05:18:06,780
It's just that I don't think
I could ever write anything

6060
05:18:06,863 --> 05:18:08,030
that comes close to doing that.

6061
05:18:08,113 --> 05:18:10,446
- Come on, that's not true.
- No, it is.

6062
05:18:12,280 --> 05:18:14,446
I-I can't do what you do.

6063
05:18:15,405 --> 05:18:16,280
Letting people in.

6064
05:18:16,363 --> 05:18:17,988
- Hannah--
- No, it's okay.

6065
05:18:18,071 --> 05:18:21,655
Um, I made a mistake trying to do this.

6066
05:18:21,738 --> 05:18:24,988
Anyway, uh, it's been an honor
to be a part of your class.

6067
05:18:25,071 --> 05:18:26,571
I really hope we can keep in touch.

6068
05:18:26,655 --> 05:18:29,905
Not on my student email,
because if I don't do the showcase,

6069
05:18:29,988 --> 05:18:32,821
then I-- I won't be here
next semester, but, um...

6070
05:18:32,905 --> 05:18:35,780
I'll send you my old one.
It's a Yahoo, for some reason.

6071
05:18:35,863 --> 05:18:37,071
[Daveed]
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Hold up.

6072
05:18:37,155 --> 05:18:38,738
Hannah, Hannah, Hannah,
Hannah, Hannah.

6073
05:18:38,821 --> 05:18:43,321
Just, if you don't come back here
right now, okay?

6074
05:18:44,113 --> 05:18:48,780
I'm still your advisor for as long
as you're here, so, talk to me.

6075
05:18:48,863 --> 05:18:51,030
Get your money's worth.
[exhales]

6076
05:18:51,571 --> 05:18:53,488
I have been doing this a while.

6077
05:18:56,696 --> 05:18:58,113
I mean...

6078
05:18:59,530 --> 05:19:00,863
Like, doesn't it hurt?

6079
05:19:01,738 --> 05:19:02,738
Doesn't what hurt?

6080
05:19:03,946 --> 05:19:07,571
Ripping yourself open over and over again.

6081
05:19:08,613 --> 05:19:11,905
Letting people see all the weird,
jagged pieces of you.

6082
05:19:13,113 --> 05:19:14,363
Is that what it feels like?

6083
05:19:14,446 --> 05:19:16,321
Yeah, well, it doesn't feel good.

6084
05:19:17,571 --> 05:19:20,655
I don't subscribe to the notion
that art has to be painful.

6085
05:19:20,738 --> 05:19:23,030
In fact, if done right,

6086
05:19:23,113 --> 05:19:25,571
allowing people into our truth,

6087
05:19:25,655 --> 05:19:27,238
that can even be healing.

6088
05:19:27,321 --> 05:19:29,571
Yeah, I don't-- I don't know about that.

6089
05:19:32,821 --> 05:19:35,571
In-- In my experience,

6090
05:19:35,655 --> 05:19:39,363
whenever I tell someone my truth, it...

6091
05:19:39,446 --> 05:19:40,446
it ends badly.

6092
05:19:43,821 --> 05:19:46,405
Well, that doesn't mean we have
to close ourselves off for good.

6093
05:19:46,488 --> 05:19:47,738
It doesn't?

6094
05:19:47,821 --> 05:19:52,696
No, that just means we have to cling
to the people who see us and smile.

6095
05:19:53,613 --> 05:19:56,446
There has to be someone like that
in your life, right?

6096
05:19:56,530 --> 05:19:58,405
[soft, tender music playing]

6097
05:20:02,988 --> 05:20:05,821
Yeah, yeah, yeah, there is.

6098
05:20:05,905 --> 05:20:09,613
Then, with love, what the hell
are you doing here talking to me?

6099
05:20:09,696 --> 05:20:11,613
- [laughs]
- Taking up my rehearsal time.

6100
05:20:11,696 --> 05:20:13,863
[laughs] Yeah, you're--
You're right.

6101
05:20:13,946 --> 05:20:16,155
Sorry. Um, I'm gonna...

6102
05:20:19,613 --> 05:20:20,988
Thank you. Thank you, Daveed.

6103
05:20:21,988 --> 05:20:22,905
Anytime.

6104
05:20:29,405 --> 05:20:31,155
- [voicemail beeps]
- [Garrett] <i>Hey, hey, it's me.</i>

6105
05:20:31,238 --> 05:20:33,030
<i>Um, are-- are you okay?</i>

6106
05:20:33,113 --> 05:20:36,071
<i>Or did I-- did I do something wrong?</i>

6107
05:20:36,155 --> 05:20:38,988
<i>Just, you said you were coming,
and you're not here.</i>

6108
05:20:39,071 --> 05:20:43,321
<i>And I-I really wish you were here.</i>

6109
05:20:44,405 --> 05:20:46,655
<i>You always help me
get out of my head, and...</i>

6110
05:20:48,530 --> 05:20:50,988
<i>I could just really use a Coach Wellsy</i>

6111
05:20:51,071 --> 05:20:53,113
pep talk right now, so...

6112
05:20:53,196 --> 05:20:55,946
Yeah, just...

6113
05:20:56,030 --> 05:20:58,780
Uh, if you could just
let me know you're okay.

6114
05:21:00,946 --> 05:21:01,988
I'm here.

6115
05:21:04,655 --> 05:21:05,571
Okay.

6116
05:21:06,238 --> 05:21:08,863
[crowd cheering]

6117
05:21:08,946 --> 05:21:11,280
Heavy into the second.
Briar's trailing 3-1.

6118
05:21:11,363 --> 05:21:14,155
You can tell Graham is frustrated
with this incessant coverage.

6119
05:21:14,238 --> 05:21:16,238
- Move it!
- Fuck you!

6120
05:21:16,988 --> 05:21:18,655
Up, G.

6121
05:21:18,738 --> 05:21:20,655
- You got Logan!
- Come on, man! Get rid of it!

6122
05:21:20,738 --> 05:21:22,905
- You got Logan! Move it!
- Heads up, G!

6123
05:21:23,405 --> 05:21:25,280
- Can't keep up, Daddy's boy?
- Fuck!

6124
05:21:25,363 --> 05:21:26,696
- [Delaney] Come on, then!
- [Jules] Woof.

6125
05:21:26,780 --> 05:21:29,946
Someone hold Garrett's hair back,
because he is getting sloppy.

6126
05:21:30,030 --> 05:21:31,530
[Logan] Go! Go! Go!

6127
05:21:31,613 --> 05:21:34,905
[Jules] Delaney banks the puck to himself
past Graham and breaks up the ice.

6128
05:21:34,988 --> 05:21:36,280
No! Fuck!

6129
05:21:36,363 --> 05:21:38,321
[Jules] Delaney sends the puck
behind the Hawks' net.

6130
05:21:38,405 --> 05:21:39,696
The Hawks are on their heels again.

6131
05:21:39,780 --> 05:21:41,488
The pass comes out front
to Delaney, and...

6132
05:21:45,363 --> 05:21:47,113
- [groans]
- [crowd jeering]

6133
05:21:47,196 --> 05:21:48,613
[whistle blows]

6134
05:21:49,655 --> 05:21:51,238
[player] Hey, we need the trainer!

6135
05:21:53,363 --> 05:21:56,363
[Jules]
What an absolutely brutal hit from Delaney

6136
05:21:56,446 --> 05:21:59,738
and a brutal end
to the second period for the Hawks.

6137
05:21:59,821 --> 05:22:03,280
Birdie sure got his bell rung.
Let's hope he's okay.

6138
05:22:05,821 --> 05:22:07,071
[Logan] How you doing, Birdie?

6139
05:22:07,571 --> 05:22:09,113
[Birdie] Everything's so fucking bright.

6140
05:22:09,613 --> 05:22:11,780
Okay. You're not going back in.

6141
05:22:11,863 --> 05:22:14,071
Rogers, you're up.

6142
05:22:14,155 --> 05:22:15,988
I'm gonna put you on D for the third.

6143
05:22:16,071 --> 05:22:16,988
- Me?
- Yeah.

6144
05:22:17,071 --> 05:22:19,821
Just keep your feet moving. Di Laurentis.

6145
05:22:19,905 --> 05:22:21,655
Yeah, I'll look out for him, Coach.

6146
05:22:25,446 --> 05:22:28,030
- Fuck Aaron Delaney, man.
- There's no way that was an accident.

6147
05:22:28,113 --> 05:22:29,488
He knew exactly what he was doing.

6148
05:22:29,571 --> 05:22:31,738
Okay, guys, anything can happen
in 20 minutes.

6149
05:22:31,821 --> 05:22:35,446
[Tucker] Maybe we switch to a one-two-two
trap to really cut off their outlets,

6150
05:22:35,530 --> 05:22:36,613
amp up the pressure?

6151
05:22:36,696 --> 05:22:38,071
[Logan] That won't work.

6152
05:22:38,863 --> 05:22:39,905
It doesn't matter what we do.

6153
05:22:39,988 --> 05:22:42,405
We were getting our asses kicked
before Birdie got domed.

6154
05:22:42,488 --> 05:22:44,780
- We know what the problem is.
- You got something to say?

6155
05:22:45,446 --> 05:22:47,655
You know you're locked off.
I told you to get rid of it.

6156
05:22:47,738 --> 05:22:50,196
- Logan, come on.
- No, everyone is thinking it.

6157
05:22:50,280 --> 05:22:53,030
Garrett Graham's got to do it all himself,
and now, we're down by two.

6158
05:22:53,113 --> 05:22:54,113
Stay in your lane, Josh.

6159
05:22:54,196 --> 05:22:55,405
Guys, come on. It's not that deep.

6160
05:22:55,488 --> 05:22:58,446
No, it fucking is for some of us, Dean.
It is that deep.

6161
05:22:59,113 --> 05:23:02,280
I'm not gonna let us lose this game,
because Phil Graham's son

6162
05:23:02,363 --> 05:23:04,571
gets to do whatever he fucking wants.

6163
05:23:05,488 --> 05:23:06,780
You don't know
what you're talking about.

6164
05:23:06,863 --> 05:23:08,238
- Come on.
- You gonna fight me now?

6165
05:23:08,321 --> 05:23:09,780
Hey! Calm down.

6166
05:23:10,780 --> 05:23:12,363
[Logan] We're on the same team, G.

6167
05:23:12,946 --> 05:23:14,363
Don't you get that?

6168
05:23:15,113 --> 05:23:17,405
You're not the only one
who can play hockey.

6169
05:23:17,488 --> 05:23:19,488
You're not the only one
who's been busting their ass,

6170
05:23:19,571 --> 05:23:22,488
and you're not the only one who wants
to beat these motherfuckers!

6171
05:23:25,946 --> 05:23:27,696
We are on the same team!

6172
05:23:27,780 --> 05:23:29,238
Logan, just give him a second
to calm down.

6173
05:23:29,321 --> 05:23:30,988
I don't need your fucking help, Tucker.

6174
05:23:32,905 --> 05:23:35,155
[breathes deeply]

6175
05:23:36,405 --> 05:23:39,321
[tense music playing]

6176
05:23:41,321 --> 05:23:42,238
Fuck.

6177
05:23:51,655 --> 05:23:52,530
[sighs]

6178
05:23:58,405 --> 05:24:00,155
- Hey.
- [door closes]

6179
05:24:00,988 --> 05:24:01,946
[sighs]

6180
05:24:02,030 --> 05:24:03,405
Need a pep talk?

6181
05:24:04,405 --> 05:24:05,613
What's going on?

6182
05:24:05,696 --> 05:24:07,071
Are you okay? Where were you?

6183
05:24:07,155 --> 05:24:08,155
I'm fine.

6184
05:24:08,238 --> 05:24:10,321
- I called, but you didn't--
- No, I know. I'm...

6185
05:24:10,405 --> 05:24:11,821
I'm sorry. I should have texted.

6186
05:24:11,905 --> 05:24:15,821
I w-- I was dealing with something
that kind of took over for a minute there,

6187
05:24:15,905 --> 05:24:17,571
um, but I'm-- I'm here now.

6188
05:24:17,655 --> 05:24:19,071
You're dealing with what?
Are you okay?

6189
05:24:19,155 --> 05:24:21,405
Yeah, I'm fine. Okay?

6190
05:24:21,488 --> 05:24:26,071
Just, you know, it didn't matter
as much as being here for you.

6191
05:24:26,946 --> 05:24:28,280
[sighs]

6192
05:24:29,655 --> 05:24:31,280
Please just text me next time.

6193
05:24:32,238 --> 05:24:33,488
I was worried about you.

6194
05:24:34,155 --> 05:24:35,863
I know. I know.

6195
05:24:40,905 --> 05:24:44,446
Okay, focus up.
Graham, what's going on out there?

6196
05:24:44,530 --> 05:24:45,821
Everything.

6197
05:24:46,696 --> 05:24:48,321
I'm playing like shit,

6198
05:24:48,405 --> 05:24:51,405
getting pressured like crazy,
making stupid mistakes.

6199
05:24:51,488 --> 05:24:53,696
Everybody's counting on me
to be in control,

6200
05:24:53,780 --> 05:24:57,821
but I just got in a stupid fight
with Logan, because...

6201
05:24:59,655 --> 05:25:00,571
Your dad's here.

6202
05:25:00,655 --> 05:25:02,030
[sighs]

6203
05:25:03,363 --> 05:25:04,613
With Cindy.

6204
05:25:10,238 --> 05:25:11,363
We can't let him win.

6205
05:25:12,280 --> 05:25:13,530
It gives him power.

6206
05:25:13,613 --> 05:25:16,905
This is how we win. We just--
We show up, and we live our lives.

6207
05:25:16,988 --> 05:25:18,655
- Okay? We can do that.
- [sighs]

6208
05:25:18,738 --> 05:25:20,363
Right?

6209
05:25:20,446 --> 05:25:21,363
Yeah.

6210
05:25:22,280 --> 05:25:23,613
And as for everything else,

6211
05:25:23,696 --> 05:25:25,863
we can just start with the small stuff
and work your way up.

6212
05:25:26,530 --> 05:25:27,863
Small stuff?

6213
05:25:27,946 --> 05:25:29,738
Yeah, whatever that means for hockey.

6214
05:25:29,821 --> 05:25:32,488
I guess the small stuff
could be stop playing like shit.

6215
05:25:32,571 --> 05:25:33,821
[both laugh]

6216
05:25:33,905 --> 05:25:36,613
- Okay, yeah. I can do that.
- [chuckles]

6217
05:25:36,696 --> 05:25:39,530
Delaney's kicking my ass, though.
Guy's a fucking monster.

6218
05:25:39,613 --> 05:25:41,446
[inhales sharply and sighs]

6219
05:25:45,905 --> 05:25:46,863
Wellsy.

6220
05:25:48,613 --> 05:25:49,988
Are you sure you're okay?

6221
05:25:51,280 --> 05:25:52,530
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

6222
05:25:52,613 --> 05:25:54,196
- I'm...
- [soft, tender music playing]

6223
05:25:56,988 --> 05:25:58,238
I'm good.

6224
05:25:59,238 --> 05:26:00,446
I promise.

6225
05:26:03,113 --> 05:26:04,071
Okay.

6226
05:26:05,196 --> 05:26:06,905
[crowd cheering]

6227
05:26:16,321 --> 05:26:17,238
Hey, Graham.

6228
05:26:23,321 --> 05:26:24,613
I love you.

6229
05:26:26,363 --> 05:26:28,280
I love you, too.

6230
05:26:28,363 --> 05:26:30,363
[tender music continues]

6231
05:26:49,446 --> 05:26:51,363
[tense music plays]

6232
05:26:57,655 --> 05:27:00,155
[buzzer]

6233
05:27:00,238 --> 05:27:03,488
Graham and Delaney meet center ice,
ready to start the final period.

6234
05:27:03,571 --> 05:27:04,738
[whistle blows]

6235
05:27:09,196 --> 05:27:11,613
What? Nothing to say this time?

6236
05:27:17,446 --> 05:27:19,196
[crowd cheering]

6237
05:27:24,071 --> 05:27:25,030
[man] Delaney, you suck!

6238
05:27:25,113 --> 05:27:26,905
Hey, that hit was bullshit, man.
You all right?

6239
05:27:26,988 --> 05:27:29,071
- Yeah, yeah. Let's go.
- I got you.

6240
05:27:29,155 --> 05:27:30,863
[upbeat percussive music]

6241
05:27:32,488 --> 05:27:33,946
[Jules] Hawks in their own zone.

6242
05:27:34,030 --> 05:27:37,321
Vipers forecheck, recover the puck,
and get it back to the point.

6243
05:27:37,405 --> 05:27:39,530
Clutch deflection by Tucker
gets the puck back to Graham.

6244
05:27:39,613 --> 05:27:41,696
But can he get past Delaney?

6245
05:27:42,363 --> 05:27:45,405
Graham puts on the brakes,
spins and drops to Tucker.

6246
05:27:45,488 --> 05:27:47,696
- Tucker shoots.
- [Tucker] Yes!

6247
05:27:47,780 --> 05:27:49,363
- Scores! Hawks score!
- [crowd cheering]

6248
05:27:49,446 --> 05:27:50,696
Whoo!

6249
05:27:50,780 --> 05:27:53,113
[rock music playing]

6250
05:27:53,196 --> 05:27:55,113
Let's go! Yes!

6251
05:27:55,946 --> 05:27:57,113
Good pass, G!

6252
05:27:57,196 --> 05:27:58,196
Let's go!

6253
05:27:58,821 --> 05:28:00,613
[players cheering]

6254
05:28:04,238 --> 05:28:05,446
Whoo!

6255
05:28:05,530 --> 05:28:07,238
I like that! I like that, Tuck!

6256
05:28:07,321 --> 05:28:11,280
Okay, Briar, looks like we've decided
to get off our knees and stop sucking.

6257
05:28:23,321 --> 05:28:24,821
[whistle blows]

6258
05:28:25,738 --> 05:28:27,696
And... cut.

6259
05:28:27,780 --> 05:28:29,238
Wow. Okay.

6260
05:28:29,321 --> 05:28:32,071
Holding back tears?
I mean, such a smart choice.

6261
05:28:32,155 --> 05:28:33,655
Beau wasn't kidding.

6262
05:28:33,738 --> 05:28:37,113
You really are
a much better reader than he is.

6263
05:28:37,196 --> 05:28:39,863
And you have cuter clothes.
Thank you for this, by the way.

6264
05:28:39,946 --> 05:28:41,571
You got it. Of course.

6265
05:28:42,113 --> 05:28:45,530
God, it is just so fun to be hanging out
with someone who's, like,

6266
05:28:45,613 --> 05:28:47,446
actually doing the thing, you know?

6267
05:28:47,530 --> 05:28:50,655
You're auditioning for a TV show
on your day off from Broadway.

6268
05:28:50,738 --> 05:28:51,780
It's so chic.

6269
05:28:51,863 --> 05:28:55,321
Oh, I think you'd feel differently
if you saw me hiding my pin curls

6270
05:28:55,405 --> 05:28:58,571
under an old baseball hat
with my falsies barely hanging on.

6271
05:28:58,655 --> 05:29:01,238
Ah, you've got to know
how cool that sounds.

6272
05:29:01,321 --> 05:29:03,530
Broadway's hard, dude.

6273
05:29:03,613 --> 05:29:07,696
It's... Like, I know I'm super lucky.

6274
05:29:07,780 --> 05:29:10,780
But, oh, my God, I'm also so exhausted.

6275
05:29:10,863 --> 05:29:11,821
[laughs]

6276
05:29:11,905 --> 05:29:14,905
I don't have time for anyone.
My dating life is in shambles.

6277
05:29:16,155 --> 05:29:18,030
That, I can relate to.

6278
05:29:18,113 --> 05:29:19,321
Ooh.

6279
05:29:19,405 --> 05:29:22,405
I smell token straight boy drama
in the theater department.

6280
05:29:22,488 --> 05:29:23,821
No, it's, like...

6281
05:29:27,488 --> 05:29:30,071
Okay, well, can we still
be peers in the industry

6282
05:29:30,155 --> 05:29:31,655
even if I tell you all my messy bullshit?

6283
05:29:31,738 --> 05:29:34,363
Oh, that's literally the only way
we'll be peers in the industry.

