<i>♪To fall in love with someone else
it's such a bitter taste ♪</i>

7010
06:15:01,328 --> 06:15:05,120
<i>♪Too cold to stand I need a hand
in crawling out your grave ♪</i>

7011
06:15:05,203 --> 06:15:08,578
<i>♪So I can get up and start living ♪</i>

7012
06:15:14,286 --> 06:15:16,745
<i>♪Too busy missing you ♪</i>

7013
06:15:19,120 --> 06:15:22,453
<i>♪Too busy missing you ♪</i>

7014
06:15:24,370 --> 06:15:26,078
<i>♪Too busy missing ♪</i>

7015
06:15:26,870 --> 06:15:29,578
[playing "Baby, Now That
I've Found You" slowly]

7016
06:15:47,536 --> 06:15:50,536
[quiet, melancholic music playing]

7017
06:16:26,161 --> 06:16:27,453
[sighs]

7018
06:16:36,703 --> 06:16:38,745
<i>♪Page one ♪</i>

7019
06:16:38,828 --> 06:16:40,703
<i>♪It's just the prologue ♪</i>

7020
06:16:41,286 --> 06:16:46,120
<i>♪Setting the stage
for all that's to happen ♪</i>

7021
06:16:46,203 --> 06:16:49,828
<i>♪Then on to the first chapter ♪</i>

7022
06:16:49,911 --> 06:16:52,453
<i>♪Everyone's happy ♪</i>

7023
06:16:52,536 --> 06:16:55,870
<i>♪For shadowing impending disaster ♪</i>

7024
06:16:55,953 --> 06:16:58,245
<i>♪Then girl meets boy ♪</i>

7025
06:16:58,328 --> 06:17:00,328
<i>♪It's awkward, confusing ♪</i>

7026
06:17:00,411 --> 06:17:04,203
<i>♪Can't tell if it's love or it's hate ♪</i>

7027
06:17:04,286 --> 06:17:07,703
<i>♪When hands graze ♪</i>

7028
06:17:07,786 --> 06:17:09,828
<i>♪Reaching for something ♪</i>

7029
06:17:09,911 --> 06:17:13,578
<i>♪Forgettably dull and mundane ♪</i>

7030
06:17:13,661 --> 06:17:16,786
<i>♪Now it's a love story ♪</i>

7031
06:17:16,870 --> 06:17:19,245
<i>♪Of epic proportion ♪</i>

7032
06:17:19,328 --> 06:17:23,245
<i>♪The likes of which never's been told ♪</i>

7033
06:17:23,328 --> 06:17:27,911
<i>♪Two hearts beating as one ♪</i>

7034
06:17:27,995 --> 06:17:32,161
<i>♪Ran right into the sun ♪</i>

7035
06:17:32,703 --> 06:17:38,036
<i>♪Oh, what would I give to go back ♪</i>

7036
06:17:38,786 --> 06:17:41,578
<i>♪Back to page one ♪</i>

7037
06:17:41,661 --> 06:17:42,536
[car engine starts]

7038
06:17:44,245 --> 06:17:46,203
Hey, which light came on first?

7039
06:17:46,286 --> 06:17:47,870
[Jules] The squiggly one? I don't know.

7040
06:17:47,953 --> 06:17:49,286
The s--

7041
06:17:49,370 --> 06:17:51,620
What? Hey, could you show me?

7042
06:17:51,703 --> 06:17:54,203
I would, but I can't get oil
on my new favorite outfit.

7043
06:17:55,620 --> 06:17:56,828
No.

7044
06:17:56,911 --> 06:17:58,828
No way. No, absolutely not.

7045
06:17:59,370 --> 06:18:01,120
They sent you so much cool shit.

7046
06:18:01,203 --> 06:18:04,328
- I told you to stop opening my mail.
- That box has been in the truck for days.

7047
06:18:04,411 --> 06:18:06,620
Days. It's practically
begging to be opened.

7048
06:18:06,703 --> 06:18:08,495
And it's a good thing I did.

7049
06:18:08,578 --> 06:18:10,036
Because look what I found.

7050
06:18:12,328 --> 06:18:13,870
Who says print media's dead?

7051
06:18:15,578 --> 06:18:17,328
- Toss it.
- Absolutely not.

7052
06:18:18,036 --> 06:18:20,578
Okay, I finally found them.

7053
06:18:20,661 --> 06:18:24,286
Ian's little's best friend's girlfriend
is in American Studies with him.

7054
06:18:24,370 --> 06:18:25,453
And?

7055
06:18:25,536 --> 06:18:27,703
And I really don't think
it's a good idea, bro.

7056
06:18:27,786 --> 06:18:28,828
What's not a good idea?

7057
06:18:28,911 --> 06:18:30,745
- Don't worry about it.
- Hunter Davenport.

7058
06:18:30,828 --> 06:18:33,036
Oh. To take Birdie's spot?

7059
06:18:33,120 --> 06:18:35,161
- See what you did?
- [Jules] That'll be messy.

7060
06:18:35,245 --> 06:18:37,703
- I love it.
- Wait, why messy?

7061
06:18:37,786 --> 06:18:39,078
Well, doesn't he hate Dean?

7062
06:18:39,161 --> 06:18:40,661
Okay, I'll bite.

7063
06:18:41,661 --> 06:18:42,661
What do you know?

7064
06:18:42,745 --> 06:18:45,453
Well, they're both bougie bitches
who vacation in the Hamptons,

7065
06:18:45,536 --> 06:18:47,036
so it could be any number of things.

7066
06:18:47,120 --> 06:18:51,161
All I know for sure is Hunter
went to high school with Dean's sister.

7067
06:18:51,870 --> 06:18:53,036
Fuck. Summer?

7068
06:18:53,120 --> 06:18:54,286
[Jules] The one and only.

7069
06:18:54,370 --> 06:18:55,786
- That's not good, man.
- Look, okay, I don't care.

7070
06:18:55,870 --> 06:18:58,036
If we're gonna have a shot at fixing
Garrett's mess, we need him.

7071
06:18:58,120 --> 06:19:00,120
- You tracked him down, yeah?
- Yeah.

7072
06:19:00,203 --> 06:19:01,328
Good.

7073
06:19:02,120 --> 06:19:02,995
Let's reach out.

7074
06:19:04,328 --> 06:19:05,828
[guitar being played]

7075
06:19:06,745 --> 06:19:10,161
<i>♪Spare myself of this ache ♪</i>

7076
06:19:11,620 --> 06:19:16,453
<i>♪How could anyone dare
to love again?♪</i>

7077
06:19:16,536 --> 06:19:19,620
<i>♪I'm raising my walls ♪</i>

7078
06:19:21,536 --> 06:19:23,703
<i>♪So I never fall ♪</i>

7079
06:19:24,953 --> 06:19:29,411
<i>♪Into another love story ♪</i>

7080
06:19:30,120 --> 06:19:31,828
[laughs] Hi.

7081
06:19:31,911 --> 06:19:33,995
What is that? It's beautiful.

7082
06:19:35,328 --> 06:19:38,578
Uh, it's just a song I wrote
in high school.

7083
06:19:39,245 --> 06:19:41,078
- Okay, Taylor Swift.
- [Hannah chuckles]

7084
06:19:41,911 --> 06:19:43,203
Those lyrics are insane.

7085
06:19:45,370 --> 06:19:47,661
Uh, yeah, well, they used to be easier.

7086
06:19:48,620 --> 06:19:49,953
I felt things.

7087
06:19:50,036 --> 06:19:51,161
I wrote them.

7088
06:19:52,161 --> 06:19:56,495
Well, some of the best songs ever
were written after a breakup.

7089
06:19:57,620 --> 06:19:59,995
Maybe this is what you need
to bust through your writer's block.

7090
06:20:01,036 --> 06:20:02,120
Yeah, I...

7091
06:20:03,453 --> 06:20:06,453
I-I think it's about more
than that, actually.

7092
06:20:10,203 --> 06:20:11,078
Yeah?

7093
06:20:13,078 --> 06:20:14,245
Yeah.

7094
06:20:23,286 --> 06:20:24,453
[clears throat]

7095
06:20:25,495 --> 06:20:26,536
[Hannah sighs]

7096
06:20:27,328 --> 06:20:28,495
Um...

7097
06:20:32,786 --> 06:20:35,536
Um, you know when you meet someone,

7098
06:20:36,745 --> 06:20:39,578
and you don't quite
get their name at first,

7099
06:20:39,661 --> 06:20:43,411
then you start seeing them all the time,
and you've got inside jokes,

7100
06:20:43,495 --> 06:20:46,286
and it just becomes really awkward
to ask what their name is?

7101
06:20:46,370 --> 06:20:49,203
- My literal nightmare, yes. Go on.
- Um...

7102
06:20:52,536 --> 06:20:53,578
Uh...

7103
06:20:56,161 --> 06:20:59,245
What if it's your best friend?

7104
06:21:00,245 --> 06:21:05,495
And she doesn't know
this huge fundamental thing about you?

7105
06:21:07,536 --> 06:21:08,411
Okay.

7106
06:21:09,995 --> 06:21:11,578
I'm gonna tell you something.

7107
06:21:12,203 --> 06:21:14,328
But I really don't want you
to look at me differently.

7108
06:21:14,411 --> 06:21:17,370
Or treat me differently.
Or hate me for not telling you sooner.

7109
06:21:17,453 --> 06:21:18,453
Hey, I would never.

7110
06:21:18,536 --> 06:21:21,536
You say that, but a lot of people did.

7111
06:21:24,495 --> 06:21:25,745
[sighs]

7112
06:21:28,286 --> 06:21:31,578
Remember my friend from high school?

7113
06:21:33,411 --> 06:21:34,536
The one who was roofied,

7114
06:21:34,620 --> 06:21:38,911
and all the stuff that happened after?

7115
06:21:44,953 --> 06:21:46,411
You're the friend.

7116
06:21:49,203 --> 06:21:51,495
Oh, Hannah, I always knew.

7117
06:21:51,578 --> 06:21:52,870
I just...

7118
06:21:54,495 --> 06:21:56,661
I thought you'd tell me
when you were ready.

7119
06:21:59,453 --> 06:22:00,495
[gasps]

7120
06:22:04,203 --> 06:22:05,495
[laughs]

7121
06:22:08,245 --> 06:22:10,536
You're my favorite person ever.

7122
06:22:10,620 --> 06:22:11,995
Right back at you, babe.

7123
06:22:13,453 --> 06:22:15,745
So, what does this have to do
with writer's block?

7124
06:22:15,828 --> 06:22:20,036
I... I just haven't been able
to write lyrics since.

7125
06:22:20,120 --> 06:22:21,203
Oh.

7126
06:22:21,786 --> 06:22:23,995
I didn't want to be the girl
who was raped.

7127
06:22:25,870 --> 06:22:27,495
I want to be this girl.

7128
06:22:28,453 --> 06:22:29,911
The girl who wrote this song.

7129
06:22:33,661 --> 06:22:37,411
The Hannah that I love is that girl.

7130
06:22:40,161 --> 06:22:41,495
And this girl.

7131
06:22:42,995 --> 06:22:44,911
And all the girls in between.

7132
06:22:45,786 --> 06:22:48,120
Because you're not just one thing, babe.

7133
06:22:48,203 --> 06:22:49,786
You're everything.

7134
06:22:51,703 --> 06:22:53,036
Never forget that.

7135
06:22:53,120 --> 06:22:56,328
Okay, you are everything.

7136
06:22:57,536 --> 06:22:59,161
[cries]

7137
06:23:02,120 --> 06:23:03,786
And the words will come when they come.

7138
06:23:10,453 --> 06:23:12,870
[laughs, sniffles]

7139
06:23:13,620 --> 06:23:18,328
And maybe I might have the beginnings

7140
06:23:18,411 --> 06:23:21,495
of an inkling of an idea for a new song.

7141
06:23:21,995 --> 06:23:24,036
But I need someone's help for it.

7142
06:23:26,870 --> 06:23:28,620
Thank you, again, for all the help.

7143
06:23:28,703 --> 06:23:29,953
Yeah, of course.

7144
06:23:30,036 --> 06:23:33,161
- Can't wait to hear the finished product.
- Yeah, if it ever turns into anything.

7145
06:23:33,953 --> 06:23:35,578
Well, hey, if it does,

7146
06:23:35,661 --> 06:23:37,661
I've got some friends
who work at the radio station.

7147
06:23:37,745 --> 06:23:39,453
I could call in a favor.

7148
06:23:39,536 --> 06:23:41,578
Yeah, I-I-I think this one's just for me.

7149
06:23:41,661 --> 06:23:43,745
These hockey sounds
will be so cool in the mix.

7150
06:23:43,828 --> 06:23:46,411
All right, totally, we got some good ones.

7151
06:23:46,995 --> 06:23:48,578
[somber music playing]

7152
06:23:49,911 --> 06:23:51,495
[exhales]

7153
06:23:56,411 --> 06:23:58,995
He's been sneaking in after practice.

7154
06:23:59,078 --> 06:24:02,411
Skates these pensive
little circles around the ice.

7155
06:24:02,495 --> 06:24:03,953
It's hard to watch.

7156
06:24:04,036 --> 06:24:06,703
Almost as bad
as his divorced Tom Brady stories.

7157
06:24:06,786 --> 06:24:09,036
- Yeah, those were bad.
- Yeah.

7158
06:24:12,161 --> 06:24:15,620
Yeah, I make Allie show me on her phone,
so he doesn't see.

7159
06:24:15,703 --> 06:24:17,536
My brother makes me do the same thing.

7160
06:24:17,620 --> 06:24:19,203
They aren't speaking?

7161
06:24:19,286 --> 06:24:21,870
No. They got in this big fight.

7162
06:24:21,953 --> 06:24:22,995
Apparently.

7163
06:24:23,745 --> 06:24:27,786
Anyway, send me the song
once it maybe turns into something.

7164
06:24:28,370 --> 06:24:29,453
Yeah.

7165
06:24:45,620 --> 06:24:46,620
Hey.

7166
06:24:49,745 --> 06:24:50,828
Hey.

7167
06:24:53,661 --> 06:24:55,245
Uh, why are you...

7168
06:24:55,328 --> 06:24:57,745
Uh, Jules was helping me with a song.

7169
06:24:58,911 --> 06:24:59,828
Yeah?

7170
06:25:00,953 --> 06:25:01,870
Yeah.

7171
06:25:02,995 --> 06:25:05,828
You kind of helped me come up
with the idea, so...

7172
06:25:05,911 --> 06:25:07,453
thanks, I guess.

7173
06:25:07,536 --> 06:25:09,495
[laughs]
Are you dropping a diss track or...?

7174
06:25:09,578 --> 06:25:11,411
[laughing] No.

7175
06:25:12,286 --> 06:25:14,870
No, uh, you just...

7176
06:25:16,203 --> 06:25:18,578
reminded me of who I used to be.

7177
06:25:20,286 --> 06:25:21,328
Right.

7178
06:25:23,078 --> 06:25:23,995
Well...

7179
06:25:25,703 --> 06:25:26,953
good luck at the showcase.

7180
06:25:28,370 --> 06:25:30,120
Actually, I dropped out.

7181
06:25:30,661 --> 06:25:31,536
Oh.

7182
06:25:32,870 --> 06:25:34,120
That's too bad.

7183
06:25:34,661 --> 06:25:36,495
Uh, you would have been really great.

7184
06:25:39,120 --> 06:25:40,995
- Well, I should--
- Hey, can I--

7185
06:25:41,620 --> 06:25:43,120
Sorry, what?

7186
06:25:43,203 --> 06:25:46,578
- No, it's fine.
- Garrett, I know we're...

7187
06:25:47,161 --> 06:25:48,286
You know.

7188
06:25:48,953 --> 06:25:50,120
But it's me.

7189
06:26:02,036 --> 06:26:03,661
I'm thinking about quitting.

7190
06:26:05,203 --> 06:26:06,411
Hockey?

7191
06:26:06,495 --> 06:26:07,703
Yeah.

7192
06:26:09,620 --> 06:26:10,870
Oh.

7193
06:26:12,370 --> 06:26:14,411
I don't know if I'm in it
for the right reasons.

7194
06:26:16,036 --> 06:26:19,161
I don't know if I'm playing because
I want to prove that I'm not like my dad

7195
06:26:19,245 --> 06:26:22,078
or I want to prove
that I <i>am</i> like my dad or...

7196
06:26:22,161 --> 06:26:24,286
[inhales deeply and sighs]

7197
06:26:24,370 --> 06:26:27,036
...because I'm not good at anything else.

7198
06:26:27,120 --> 06:26:28,370
But...

7199
06:26:31,620 --> 06:26:34,661
Jensen said I should be skating
because I love it, and...

7200
06:26:37,536 --> 06:26:38,578
I don't know.

7201
06:26:42,245 --> 06:26:44,786
You once told me

7202
06:26:45,328 --> 06:26:48,495
that you'd be relieved
if you couldn't play anymore.

7203
06:26:50,078 --> 06:26:51,328
And now, you can't.

7204
06:26:52,578 --> 06:26:55,745
And that means you could be anywhere,
doing anything.

7205
06:26:56,745 --> 06:26:58,036
But you're not.

7206
06:26:59,536 --> 06:27:00,661
You're here.

7207
06:27:01,370 --> 06:27:02,286
On the ice.

7208
06:27:02,370 --> 06:27:03,495
Skating.

7209
06:27:08,703 --> 06:27:12,203
And for what it's worth,
you do have a good reason to play.

7210
06:27:13,745 --> 06:27:14,828
It's not your dad.

7211
06:27:15,953 --> 06:27:17,328
It's the guy on your right.

7212
06:27:17,995 --> 06:27:19,578
Who's always had your back.

7213
06:27:21,370 --> 06:27:23,078
Even when you're being an asshole.

7214
06:27:33,370 --> 06:27:34,536
[sniffles]

7215
06:27:40,703 --> 06:27:42,078
[crowd cheering]

7216
06:27:43,828 --> 06:27:44,828
[Garrett] <i>Come! Come here!</i>

7217
06:27:44,911 --> 06:27:46,495
- [Logan] <i>Right here!</i>
- [puck clangs off goalpost]

7218
06:27:46,578 --> 06:27:48,495
- [buzzer]
- [Garrett] <i>Yes, yes!</i>

7219
06:27:57,536 --> 06:27:59,078
[sniffles]

7220
06:28:00,620 --> 06:28:01,786
[crowd shouting]

7221
06:28:01,870 --> 06:28:04,495
[Jules] <i>Graham and Logan
have been having a blast out there.</i>

7222
06:28:04,578 --> 06:28:07,828
<i>We love that for them.
And more importantly, we love it for me.</i>

7223
06:28:07,911 --> 06:28:09,036
[laughs]

7224
06:28:09,120 --> 06:28:10,995
[indistinct shouting and cheers]

7225
06:28:13,286 --> 06:28:14,745
[Jules] <i>Two minutes left, it's looking--</i>

7226
06:28:15,328 --> 06:28:17,786
<i>...Graham and Delaney meet center ice,
ready to start the--</i>

7227
06:28:17,870 --> 06:28:19,245
[skate blades on ice]

7228
06:28:27,245 --> 06:28:29,036
[yells]

7229
06:28:40,745 --> 06:28:42,370
[Logan] <i>Hey, get off!</i>

7230
06:28:42,453 --> 06:28:44,120
- [whistle blows]
<i>- Get off of him!</i>

7231
06:28:44,203 --> 06:28:46,411
[Logan] <i>Hey! Graham!</i>

7232
06:28:47,411 --> 06:28:49,828
- Hey! Hey!
- [Garret grunts]

7233
06:28:49,911 --> 06:28:51,578
- Bring him to me! Come here!
- Hey! Hey!

7234
06:28:52,370 --> 06:28:53,578
Garrett, look at me!

7235
06:28:53,661 --> 06:28:55,036
- [panting]
- Hey, I got you.

7236
06:28:57,620 --> 06:28:58,661
I got you.

7237
06:28:59,703 --> 06:29:00,620
Okay?

7238
06:29:05,995 --> 06:29:07,411
[tap water running]

7239
06:29:12,870 --> 06:29:15,495
Oh, you know Tucker hates
when you do that in the kitchen.

7240
06:29:16,495 --> 06:29:18,370
[scoffs] He'll live.

7241
06:29:23,620 --> 06:29:24,703
What do you want, Garrett?

7242
06:29:29,411 --> 06:29:30,620
The, uh...

7243
06:29:31,453 --> 06:29:32,661
St. A's game.

7244
06:29:35,661 --> 06:29:37,745
You pulled me off Delaney.

7245
06:29:39,495 --> 06:29:40,370
Yeah.

7246
06:29:42,661 --> 06:29:43,661
Thank you.

7247
06:29:47,036 --> 06:29:48,453
I blacked out.

7248
06:29:51,786 --> 06:29:53,328
If you hadn't stopped me...

7249
06:29:57,453 --> 06:29:59,286
Listen, Delaney's a piece of shit.

7250
06:30:00,411 --> 06:30:01,911
But I don't want to be that guy.

7251
06:30:03,370 --> 06:30:07,370
I don't want to be the guy
who loses himself in a violent rage.

7252
06:30:09,370 --> 06:30:10,578
I don't want to be...

7253
06:30:14,120 --> 06:30:15,411
[sighs]

7254
06:30:19,786 --> 06:30:21,161
I don't want to be my dad.

7255
06:30:24,953 --> 06:30:26,120
Look, um...

7256
06:30:28,578 --> 06:30:30,161
I'm gonna say some things.

7257
06:30:31,286 --> 06:30:33,536
I haven't said
any of this out loud before.

